225 464 173 (ERA afn) 173 SB
225 582 1926 (The ERA \(erase\) command removes files from the currently logged-in disk, for example, the disk) 1926 SB
225 641 1933 (name currently prompted by CP/M preceding the >. The files that are erased are those that satisfy) 1933 SB
225 700 1663 ( the ambiguous file reference afn. The following examples illustrate the use of ERA:) 1663 SB
225 819 197 (ERA X.Y) 197 SB
675 819 1480 (The file named X.Y on the currently logged disk is removed from the disk ) 1480 SB
675 878 697 (directory and the space is returned.) 697 SB
225 937 715 (                                                       ) 715 SB
225 996 186 (ERA X.*) 186 SB
675 996 1289 (All files with primary name X are removed from the current disk.) 1289 SB
225 1115 257 (ERA *.ASM) 257 SB
675 1115 1407 (All files with secondary name ASM are removed from the current disk.) 1407 SB
225 1233 316 (ERA X?Y.C?M) 316 SB
675 1233 1493 (All files on the current disk that satisfy the ambiguous reference X?Y.C?M ) 1493 SB
675 1292 230 (are deleted.) 230 SB
225 1410 175 (ERA *.*) 175 SB
675 1410 1355 (Erase all files on the current disk. In this case, the CCP prompts the ) 1355 SB
675 1470 504 (console with the message) 504 SB
675 1588 395 (ALL FILES \(Y/N\)?) 395 SB
675 1706 1232 (which requires a Y response before files are actually removed.) 1232 SB
225 1825 294 (ERA B:*.PRN) 294 SB
675 1825 1477 (All files on drive B that satisfy the ambiguous reference ????????.PRN are ) 1477 SB
675 1884 1017 (deleted, independently of the currently logged disk.) 1017 SB
