225 1115 1797 (The operator precedes either ufn1 or ufn2 \(or both\) by an optional drive address. If ufn1 is) 1797 SB
225 1174 1867 (preceded by a drive name, then ufn2 is assumed to exist on the same drive. Similarly, if ufn2 is) 1867 SB
225 1233 1941 (preceded by a drive name, then ufn1 is assumed to exist on the drive as well. The same drive must) 1941 SB
225 1292 1925 (be specified in both cases if both ufn1 and ufn2 are preceded by drive names. The following REN) 1925 SB
225 1351 638 (commands illustrate this format:) 638 SB
225 1470 502 (REN A:X.ASM=Y.ASM) 502 SB
975 1470 1001 (The file Y.ASM is changed to X.ASM on drive A.) 1001 SB
225 1588 596 (REN B:ZAP.BAS=ZOT.BAS) 596 SB
975 1588 1095 (The file ZOT.BAS is changed to ZAP.BAS on drive B.) 1095 SB
225 1706 541 (REN B:A.ASM=B:A.BAK) 541 SB
975 1706 998 (The file A.BAK is renamed to A.ASM on drive B.) 998 SB
