225 464 244 (SAVE n ufn) 244 SB
225 582 1879 (The SAVE command places n pages \(256-byte blocks\) onto disk from the TPA and names this) 1879 SB
225 641 1826 (file ufn. In the CP/M distribution system, the TPA starts at 100H \(hexadecimal\) which is the) 1826 SB
225 700 1816 (second page of memory. The SAVE command must specify 2 pages of memory if the user's) 1816 SB
225 760 1923 (program occupies the area from 100H through 2FFH. The machine code file can be subsequently) 1923 SB
225 819 1471 (loaded and executed. The following are examples of the SAVE command:) 1471 SB
225 937 343 (SAVE 3 X.COM) 343 SB
975 937 800 (Copies 100H through 3FFH to X.COM.) 800 SB
225 1055 242 (SAVE 40 Q) 242 SB
975 1055 1188 (Copies 100H through 28FFH to Q. Note that 28 is the page) 1188 SB

