225 878 1856 (The USER command allows maintenance of separate files in the same directory. In the syntax) 1856 SB
225 937 1922 (line, n is an Integer value in the range 0 to 15. On cold start, the operator is automatically logged) 1922 SB
225 996 1939 (into user area number 0, which is compatible with standard CP/M 1 directories. You can issue the) 1939 SB
225 1055 1869 (USER command at any time to move to another logical area within the same directory. Drives) 1869 SB
225 1115 1894 (that are logged-in while addressing one user number are automatically active when the operator) 1894 SB
225 1174 1882 (moves to another. A user number is simply a prefix that accesses particular directory entries on) 1882 SB
225 1233 330 (the active disks. ) 330 SB
225 1351 1895 (The active user number is maintained until changed by a subsequent USER command, or until a) 1895 SB
225 1410 796 (cold start when user 0 is again assumed.) 796 SB
