225 227 1805 (Transient commands are specified in the same manner as built-in commands, and additional) 1805 SB
225 286 1766 (commands are easily defined by the user. For convenience, the transient command can be) 1766 SB
225 345 1940 (preceded by a drive name which causes the transient to be loaded from the specified drive into the) 1940 SB
225 405 788 (TPA for execution. Thus, the command) 788 SB
225 523 172 (B:STAT) 172 SB
225 582 13 ( ) 13 SB
225 641 1906 (causes CP/M to temporarily log in drive B for the source of the STAT transient, and then return) 1906 SB
225 700 1061 (to the original logged disk for subsequent processing.) 1061 SB
