375 1115 454 (STAT "command line") 454 SB
225 1233 1784 (The STAT command provides general statistical information about file storage and device) 1784 SB
225 1292 1767 (assignment. Special forms of the command line allow the current device assignment to be) 1767 SB
225 1351 1780 (examined and altered. The various command lines that can be specified are shown with an) 1780 SB
225 1410 740 (explanation of each form to the right.) 740 SB
225 1529 190 (     STAT) 190 SB
525 1529 1560 (If you type an empty command line, the STAT transient calculates the storage ) 1560 SB
525 1588 1427 (remaining on all active drives, and prints one of the following messages:) 1427 SB
525 1706 460 (d: R/W, SPACE: nnnK) 460 SB
525 1825 450 (d: R/O, SPACE: nnnK) 450 SB
525 1943 1641 (for each active drive d:, where R/W indicates the drive can be read or written, and ) 1641 SB
525 2002 1623 (R/O indicates the drive is Read-Only \(a drive becomes R/O by explicitly setting it ) 1623 SB
525 2061 1492 (to Read-Only, as shown below, or by inadvertently changing disks without ) 1492 SB
525 2120 1603 (performing a warm start\). The space remaining on the disk in drive d: is given in ) 1603 SB
525 2180 336 (kilobytes by nnn.) 336 SB
225 2298 242 (     STAT d:) 242 SB
525 2298 1628 (If a drive name is given, then the drive is selected before the storage is computed. ) 1628 SB
525 2357 1635 (Thus, the command STAT B: could be issued while logged into drive A, resulting ) 1635 SB
525 2416 289 (in the message) 289 SB
525 2535 722 (BYTES REMAINING ON B: nnnK) 722 SB
