225 227 264 (     STAT afn) 264 SB
525 227 1632 (The command line can also specify a set of files to be scanned by STAT. The files ) 1632 SB
525 286 1625 (that satisfy afn are listed in alphabetical order, with storage requirements for each ) 1625 SB
525 345 442 (file under the heading:) 442 SB
525 464 830 (RECS BYTES EXT D:FILENAME.TYP) 830 SB
525 523 529 (rrrr bbbk ee d:filename.typ) 529 SB
525 641 1508 (where rrrr is the number of 128-byte records allocated to the file, bbb is the ) 1508 SB
525 700 1633 (number of kilobytes allocated to the file \(bbb=rrrr*128/1024\), ee is the number of ) 1633 SB
525 760 1528 (16K extensions \(ee=bbb/16\), d is the drive name containing the file \(A ... P\), ) 1528 SB
525 819 1557 (filename is the eight-character primary filename, and typ is the three-character ) 1557 SB
525 878 1461 (filetype. After listing the individual files, the storage usage is summarized.) 1461 SB
225 996 1791 (     STAT d:afn   The drive name can be given ahead of the afn. The specified drive is first ) 1791 SB
525 1055 897 (selected, and the form STAT afn is executed.) 897 SB
225 1174 353 (     STAT d:=R/O) 353 SB
675 1174 1476 (This form sets the drive given by d to Read-Only, remaining in effect until ) 1476 SB
525 1233 1579 (the next warm or cold start takes place. When a disk is Read-Only, the message) 1579 SB
525 1351 607 (BDOS ERR ON d: Read-Only) 607 SB
225 1410 247 (                   ) 247 SB
525 1470 1601 (appears if there is an attempt to write to the Read-Only disk. CP/M waits until a ) 1601 SB
525 1529 1616 (key is pressed before performing an automatic warm start, at which time the disk ) 1616 SB
525 1588 291 (becomes R/W.) 291 SB
225 1706 1853 (The STAT command allows you to control the physical-to-logical device assignment. See the) 1853 SB
225 1765 1866 (IOBYTE function described in Sections 5 and 6. There are four logical peripheral devices that) 1866 SB
225 1825 1784 (are, at any particular instant, each assigned one of several physical peripheral devices. The) 1784 SB
225 1884 879 (following is a list of the four logical devices:) 879 SB
375 2002 162 (- CON: ) 162 SB
675 2002 1416 (is the system console device, used by CCP for communication with the ) 1416 SB
675 2061 183 (operator.) 183 SB
375 2180 159 (- RDR: ) 159 SB
675 2180 617 (is the paper tape reader device.) 617 SB
375 2298 157 (- PUN: ) 157 SB
675 2298 612 (is the paper tape punch device.) 612 SB
375 2416 133 (- LST:) 133 SB
675 2416 473 (is the output list device.) 473 SB
225 92 498 (1.6 Transient Commands) 498 SB
