225 227 1907 (The current logical-to-physical device assignment is changed by typing a STAT command of the) 1907 SB
225 286 109 (form:) 109 SB
225 405 709 (STAT ld1=pd1,ld2=pd2,...,ldn=pdn) 709 SB
225 523 1838 (where ld1 through ldn are logical device names and pd1 through pdn are compatible physical) 1838 SB
225 582 1875 (device names. For example, ld1 and pd1 appear on the same line in the VAL: command shown) 1875 SB
225 641 1690 (above.  The following example shows valid STAT commands that change the current) 1690 SB
225 700 770 (logical-to-physical device assignments:) 770 SB
225 819 396 (STAT CON:=CRT:) 396 SB
225 878 894 (STAT PUN:=TTY:,LST:=LPT:,RDR:=TTY) 894 SB
225 996 404 (The command form,) 404 SB
225 1115 485 (STAT d:filename.typ $S) 485 SB
225 1233 1877 (where d: is an optional drive name and filename.typ is an unambiguous or ambiguous filename,) 1877 SB
225 1292 910 (produces the following output display format:) 910 SB
225 1410 844 (         Size      Recs      Bytes         Ext Acc) 844 SB
225 1529 978 (            48        48         6K     1 R/O A:ED.COM) 978 SB
225 1588 1022 (            55        55        12K     I R/O \(A:PIP.COM\)) 1022 SB
225 1647 1006 (         65536       128        16K     2 R/W A:X.DAT) 1006 SB
225 1765 1865 (where the $S parameter causes the Size field to be displayed.  Without the $S, the Size field is) 1865 SB
225 1825 1903 (skipped, but the remaining fields are displayed. The Size field lists the virtual file size in records,) 1903 SB
225 1884 1813 (while the Recs field sums the number of virtual records in each extent. For files constructed) 1813 SB
225 1943 1935 (sequentially, the Size and Recs fields are identical. The Bytes field lists the actual number of bytes) 1935 SB
225 2002 1878 (allocated to the corresponding file. The minimum allocation unit is determined at configuration) 1878 SB
225 2061 1916 (time; thus, the number of bytes corresponds to the record count plus the remaining unused space) 1916 SB
225 2120 1927 (in the last allocated block for sequential files. Random access files are given data areas only when) 1927 SB
225 2180 1831 (written, so the Bytes field contains the only accurate allocation figure. In the case of random) 1831 SB
225 2239 1860 (access, the Size field gives the logical end-of-file record position and the Recs field counts the) 1860 SB
225 2298 1942 (logical records of each extent. Each of these extents, however, can contain unallocated holes even) 1942 SB
225 2357 886 (though they are added into the record count.) 886 SB
225 92 498 (1.6 Transient Commands) 498 SB
1526 92 649 (CP/M Operating System Manual) 649 SB
1154 2942 92 (1-19) 92 SB
