225 996 703 (         0: Checked Directory Eritries) 703 SB
225 1055 514 (      1024: Records/Extent) 514 SB
225 1115 499 (       128: Records/BlocK) 499 SB
225 1174 471 (        58: Sectors/TracK) 471 SB
225 1233 512 (         2: Reserved TracKs) 512 SB
225 1351 1907 (where d: is the selected drive, followed by the total record capacity \(65536 is an eight-megabyte) 1907 SB
225 1410 1931 (drive\), followed by the total capacity listed in kilobytes. The directory size is listed next, followed) 1931 SB
225 1470 1932 (by the checked entries. The number of checked entries is usualiv identical to the directory size for) 1932 SB
225 1529 1751 (removable media, because this mechanism is used to detect changed media during CP/M) 1751 SB
225 1588 1938 (operation without an intervening warm start. For fixed media, the number is usually zero, because) 1938 SB
225 1647 1268 (the media are not changed without at least a cold or warm start.) 1268 SB
225 1765 1830 (The number of records per extent determines the addressing capacity of each directory entry) 1830 SB
225 1825 1947 (\(1024 times 128 bytes, or 128K in the previous example\). The number of records per block shows) 1947 SB
225 1884 1877 (the basic allocation size \(in the example, 128 records/block times 128 bytes per record, or 16K) 1877 SB
225 1943 1907 (bytes per block\). The listing is then followed by the number of physical sectors per track and the) 1907 SB
225 2002 530 (number of reserved tracks.) 530 SB
