225 227 1946 (For convenience, PIP allows abbreviated commands for transferring files between disk drives. The) 1946 SB
225 286 516 (abbreviated PIP forms are) 516 SB
375 405 214 (PIP d:=afn) 214 SB
375 464 303 (PIP d1:=d2:afn) 303 SB
375 523 242 (PIP ufn=d2:) 242 SB
375 582 301 (PlP d1:ufn=d2:) 301 SB
225 700 1890 (The first form copies all files from the currently logged disk that satisfy the afn to the same files) 1890 SB
225 760 1893 (on drive d, where d = A...P. The second form is equivalent to the first, where the source for the) 1893 SB
225 819 1692 (copy is drive d2 where d2 = A ... P. The third form is equivalent to the command PIP) 1692 SB
225 878 1864 (d1:ufn=d2:ufn which copies the file given by ufn from drive d2 to the file ufn on drive d1. The) 1864 SB
225 937 1675 (fourth form is equivalent to the third, where the source disk is explicitly given by d2.) 1675 SB
225 1055 1898 (The source and destination disks must be different in all of these cases. If an afn is specfied, PIP) 1898 SB
225 1115 1849 (lists each ufn that satisfies the afn as it is being copied. If a file exists by the same name as the) 1849 SB
225 1174 1904 (destination file, it is removed after successful completion of the copy and replaced by the copied) 1904 SB
225 1233 74 (file.) 74 SB
225 1351 1637 (The following PIP commands give examples of valid disk-to-disk copy operations:) 1637 SB
225 1470 277 (     B=*.COM) 277 SB
825 1470 1348 (Copies all files that have the secondary name COM to drive B from ) 1348 SB
825 1529 342 (the current drive.) 342 SB
225 1647 320 (     A:=B:ZAP.*) 320 SB
825 1647 1283 (Copies all files that have the primary name ZAP to drive A from ) 1283 SB
825 1706 159 (drive B.) 159 SB
225 1825 353 (     ZAP.ASM=B:) 353 SB
825 1825 690 (Same as ZAP.ASM=B:ZAP.ASM ) 690 SB
225 1943 412 (     B:ZOT.COM=A:) 412 SB
825 1943 746 (Same as B:ZOT.COM=A:ZOT.COM) 746 SB
225 2061 443 (     B:=GAMMA.BAS) 443 SB
825 2061 857 (Same as B:GAMMA.BAS=GAMMA.BAS) 857 SB
225 2180 492 (     B:=A:GAMMA.BAS) 492 SB
825 2180 906 (Same as B:GAMMA.BAS=A:GAMMA.BAS) 906 SB
