225 1884 1950 (   -NUL: sends 40 nulls \(ASCII 0s\) to the device. This can be issued at the end of punched output.) 1950 SB
225 2002 1935 (   -EOF: sends a CP/M end-of-file \(ASCII CTRL-Z\) to the destination device \(sent automatically ) 1935 SB
375 2061 1042 (  at the end of all ASCII data transfers through PIP\).) 1042 SB
225 2180 1944 (   -INP: is a special PIP input source that can be patched into the PIP program. PIP gets the input ) 1944 SB
375 2239 1752 ( data character-by-character, by CALLing location 103H, with data returned in location ) 1752 SB
375 2298 630 ( 109H \(parity bit must be zero\).) 630 SB
