225 227 785 (The following are valid PIP commands:) 785 SB
225 345 363 (PIP LST:=X.PRN) 363 SB
525 464 1323 (Copies X.PRN to the LST device and terminates the PIP program.) 1323 SB
225 582 73 (PIP) 73 SB
525 700 1208 (Starts PIP for a sequence of commands. PIP prompts with *.) 1208 SB
225 819 660 (*CON:=X.ASM,Y.ASM,Z.ASM) 660 SB
525 937 1214 (Concatenates three ASM files and copies to the CON device.) 1214 SB
225 1055 608 (*X.HEX=CON:,Y.HEX,PTR:) 608 SB
525 1174 1647 (Creates a HEX file by reading the CON until a CTRL-Z is typed, followed by data ) 1647 SB
525 1233 1086 (from Y.HEX and PTR until a CTRL-Z is encountered.) 1086 SB
225 1351 763 (PIP PUN:=NUL:,X.ASM,EOF:,NUL:) 763 SB
525 1470 1630 (Sends 40 nulls to the punch device; copies the X.ASM file to the punch, followed ) 1630 SB
525 1529 1141 (by an end-of-file, CTRL-Z, and 40 more  null characters. ) 1141 SB
225 1647 326 (\(carriage return\)) 326 SB
525 1765 683 (A single carriage return stops PIP.) 683 SB
