225 1410 1942 (The DESTINATION prompt is repeated until a single carriage return is pressed at the console, so) 1942 SB
225 1470 824 (that more than one disk can be initialized.) 824 SB
225 1588 1906 (Upon completion of a successful system generation, the new disk contains the operating system,) 1906 SB
225 1647 1935 (and only the built-in commands are available. An IBM-compatible disk appears to CP/M as a disk) 1935 SB
225 1706 1868 (with an empty directory; therefore, the operator must copy the appropriate COM files from an) 1868 SB
225 1765 1450 (existing CP/M disk to the newly constructed disk using the PIP transient.) 1450 SB
