225 227 549 (1.6.7 SUBMIT Command) 549 SB
32 0 0 50 50 1 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 345 150 (Syntax:) 150 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
375 464 632 (SUBMIT ufn parm#l ... parm#n) 632 SB
225 582 1946 (The SUBMIT command allows CP/M commands to be batched for automatic processing. The ufn) 1946 SB
225 641 1910 (given in the SUBMIT command must be the filename of a file that exists on the currently logged) 1910 SB
225 700 1899 (disk, with an assumed file type of SUB. The SUB file contains CP/M prototype commands with) 1899 SB
225 760 1939 (possible parameter substitution.  The actual parameters parm#1 ... parm#n are substituted into the) 1939 SB
225 819 1841 (prototype commands, and, if no errors occur, the file of substituted commands are processed) 1841 SB
225 878 438 (sequentially by CP/M.) 438 SB
225 996 1908 (The prototype command file is created using the ED program, with interspersed $ parameters of) 1908 SB
225 1055 183 (the form:) 183 SB
375 1174 293 ($1 $2 $3 ... Sn) 293 SB
225 1292 1921 (corresponding to the number of actual parameters that will be included when the file is submitted) 1921 SB
225 1351 1926 (for execution. When the SUBMIT transient is executed, the actual parameters parm#1 ... parm#n) 1926 SB
225 1410 1843 (are paired with the formal parameters $1 ... $n in the prototype commands. If the numbers of) 1843 SB
225 1470 1897 (formal and actual parameters do not correspond, the SUBMIT function is aborted with an error) 1897 SB
225 1529 1878 (message at the console. The SUBMIT function creates a file of substituted commands with the) 1878 SB
225 1588 105 (name) 105 SB
225 1706 185 ($$$.SUB) 185 SB
225 1825 1900 (on the logged disk. When the system reboots, at the termination of the SUBMIT, this command) 1900 SB
225 1884 1866 (file is read by the CCP as a source of input rather than the console. If the SUBMIT function is) 1866 SB
225 1943 1808 (performed on any disk other than drive A, the commands are not processed until the disk is) 1808 SB
225 2002 1907 (inserted into drive A and the system reboots. You can abort command processing at any time by) 1907 SB
225 2061 1896 (pressing the rubout key when the command is read and echoed. In this case, the $$$.SUB file is) 1896 SB
225 2120 1845 (removed and the subsequent commands come from the console. Command processing is also) 1845 SB
225 2180 1922 (aborted if the CCP detects an error in any of the commands.  Programs that execute under CP/M) 1922 SB
225 2239 1798 (can abort processing of command files when error conditions occur by erasing any existing) 1798 SB
225 2298 272 ($$$.SUB file.) 272 SB
225 2416 1825 (To introduce dollar signs into a SUBMIT file, you can type a $$ which reduces to a single $) 1825 SB
225 2475 1888 (within the command file. An up arrow, ^|, precedes an alphabetic character s, which produces a) 1888 SB
225 2535 800 (single CTRL-X character within the file.) 800 SB
