225 227 1912 (An additional utility program called XSUB extends the power of the SUBMIT facility to include) 1912 SB
225 286 1932 (line input to programs as well as the CCP. The XSUB command is included as the first line of the) 1932 SB
225 345 1906 (SUBMIT file. When it is executed, XSUB self-relocates directly below the CCP. All subsequent) 1906 SB
225 405 1865 (SUBMIT command lines are processed by XSUB so that programs that read buffered console) 1865 SB
225 464 1948 (input, BDOS Function 10, receive their input directly from the SUBMIT file. For example, the file) 1948 SB
225 523 1105 (SAVER.SUB can contain the following SUBMIT lines:) 1105 SB
225 641 133 (XSUB) 133 SB
225 700 103 (DDT) 103 SB
225 760 206 (I $1.COM) 206 SB
225 819 33 (R) 33 SB
225 878 61 (G0) 61 SB
225 937 357 (SAVE 1 $2.COM) 357 SB
225 1055 833 (a subsequent SUBMIT command, such as) 833 SB
225 1174 549 (A:SUBMIT SAVER PIP Y) 549 SB
225 1292 1919 (substitutes PIP for $1 and Y for $2 in the command stream. The XSUB program loads, followed) 1919 SB
225 1351 1873 (by DDT, which is sent to the command lines PIP.COM, R, and G0, thus returning to the CCP.) 1873 SB
225 1410 1258 (The final command SAVE 1 Y.COM is processed by the CCP. ) 1258 SB
375 1529 1257 (The XSUB program remains in memory and prints the message) 1257 SB
225 1647 256 (\(xsub active\)) 256 SB
225 1765 1887 (on each warm start operation to indicate its presence.  Subsequent SUBMIT command streams) 1887 SB
225 1825 1813 (do not require the XSUB, unless an intervening cold start occurs. Note that XSUB must be) 1813 SB
225 1884 1663 (loaded after the optional CP/M DESPOOL utility, if both are to run simultaneously.) 1663 SB
