375 464 221 (MOVCPM) 221 SB
225 582 1898 (The MOVCPM program allows you to reconfigure the CP/M system for any particular memory) 1898 SB
225 641 1911 (size. Two optional parameters can be used to indicate the desired size of the new system and the) 1911 SB
225 700 1898 (disposition of the new system at program termination. If the first parameter is omitted or an * is) 1898 SB
225 760 1824 (given, the MOVCPM program reconfigures the system to its maximum size, based upon the) 1824 SB
225 819 1866 (kilobytes of contigous RAM in the host system \(starting at 0000H\). If the second parameter is) 1866 SB
225 878 1894 (omitted, the system is executed, but not permanently recorded; if * is given, the system is left in) 1894 SB
225 937 1917 (memory, ready for a SYSGEN operation. The MOVCPM program relocates a memory image of) 1917 SB
225 996 1846 (CP/M and places this image in memory in preparation for a system generation operation. The) 1846 SB
225 1055 973 (following is a list of MOVCPM command forms:) 973 SB
225 1174 286 (     MOYCPM) 286 SB
675 1174 1398 (Relocates and executes CP/M for management of the current memory ) 1398 SB
675 1233 1368 (configuration \(memory is examined for contiguous RAM, starting at ) 1368 SB
675 1292 1441 (100H\). On completion of the relocation, the new system is executed but ) 1441 SB
675 1351 1383 (not permanently recorded on the disk. The system that is constructed ) 1383 SB
675 1410 796 (contains a BIOS for the Intel MDS 800.) 796 SB
225 1529 323 (     MOVCPM n) 323 SB
675 1529 1478 (Creates a relocated CP/M system for management of an n kilobyte system ) 1478 SB
675 1588 1477 (\(n must be in the range of 20 to 64\), and executes the system as described.) 1477 SB
225 1706 362 (     MOYCPM * *) 362 SB
675 1706 1240 (Constructs a relocated memory image for the current memory ) 1240 SB
675 1765 1488 (configuration, but leaves the memory image in memory in preparation for a) 1488 SB
675 1825 410 (SYSGEN operation.) 410 SB
225 1943 361 (     MOYCPM n *) 361 SB
675 1943 1440 (Constructs a relocated memory image for an n kilobyte memory system, ) 1440 SB
675 2002 1403 (and leaves the memory image in preparation for a SYSGEN operation.) 1403 SB
225 92 498 (1.6 Transient Commands) 498 SB
