225 227 553 (For example, the command,) 553 SB
225 345 297 (MOVCPM * *) 297 SB
225 464 1830 (constructs a new version of the CP/M system and leaves it in memory, ready for a SYSGEN) 1830 SB
225 523 471 (operation. The message) 471 SB
225 641 586 (READY FOR 'SYSGEN' OR) 586 SB
225 700 501 ('SAYE 34 CPMxx.COM') 501 SB
225 819 1884 (appears at the console upon completion, where xx is the current memory size in kilobytes. You) 1884 SB
225 878 747 (can then type the following sequence:) 747 SB
225 996 351 (SYSGEN            ) 351 SB
975 996 663 (This starts the system generation.) 663 SB
225 1115 535 (SOURCE DRIVE NAME ) 535 SB
975 1115 1166 (Respond with a carriage return to skip the CP/M read \(OR) 1166 SB
225 1174 418 (RETURN TO SKIP\)) 418 SB
975 1174 1119 (operation, because the system is already in memory as a ) 1119 SB
975 1233 870 (result of the previous MOVCPM operation.) 870 SB
225 1351 685 (DESTINATION DRIVE NAME  ) 685 SB
975 1351 1175 (Respond with B to write new system to the disk in drive B.) 1175 SB
225 1410 592 (OR RETURN TO REBOOT\)) 592 SB
975 1410 940 (SYSGEN prompts with the following message:) 940 SB
225 1529 478 (DESTINATION ON B,) 478 SB
975 1529 1160 (Place the new disk on drive B and press the RETURN key) 1160 SB
225 1588 486 (THEN TYPE RETURN) 486 SB
975 1588 241 (when ready.) 241 SB
225 1706 1778 (If you respond with A rather than B above, the system is written to drive A rather than B.) 1778 SB
225 1765 812 (SYSGEN continues to print this prompt:) 812 SB
225 1884 1281 (DESTINATION DRIVE NAME \(OR RETURN TO REBOOT\)) 1281 SB
225 2002 1921 (until you respond with a single carriage return, which stops the SYSGEN program with a system) 1921 SB
225 2061 143 (reboot.) 143 SB
