225 227 1883 (The BAD SECTOR message indicates that the disk controller electronics has detected an error) 1883 SB
225 286 1871 (condition in reading or writing the disk. This condition is generally caused by a malfunctioning) 1871 SB
225 345 1943 (disk controller or an extremely worn disk. If you find that CP/M reports this error more than once) 1943 SB
225 405 1921 (a month, the state of the controller electronics and the condition of the media should be checked.) 1921 SB
225 523 1857 (You can also encounter this condition in reading files generated by a controller produced by a) 1857 SB
225 582 1849 (different manufacturer.  Even though controllers claim to be IBM compatible, one often finds) 1849 SB
225 641 1920 (small differences in recording formats. The MDS-800 controller, for example, requires two bytes) 1920 SB
225 700 1909 (of ones following the data CRC byte, which is not required in the IBM format. As a result, disks) 1909 SB
225 760 1905 (generated by the Intel MDS can be read by almost all other IBM-compatible systems, while disk) 1905 SB
225 819 1859 (files generated on other manufacturers' equipment produce the BAD SECTOR message when) 1859 SB
225 878 1917 (read by the MDS. To recover from this condition, press a CTRL-C to reboot \(the safest course\),) 1917 SB
225 937 1217 (or a return, which ignores the bad sector in the file operation.) 1217 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c356 font
225 1055 117 (Note:) 117 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
342 1056 1768 (pressing a return might destroy disk integrity if the operation is a directory write. Be sure) 1768 SB
225 1116 805 (you have adequate back-ups in this case.) 805 SB
225 1234 1747 (The SELECT error occurs when there is an attempt to address a drive beyond the range) 1747 SB
225 1293 1906 (supported by the BIOS. In this case, the value of d in the error message gives the selected drive.) 1906 SB
225 1352 1143 (The system reboots following any input from the console.) 1143 SB
225 1471 1847 (The READ ONLY message occurs when there is an attempt to write to a disk or file that has) 1847 SB
225 1530 1907 (been designated as Read-Only in a STAT command or has been set to Read-Only by the BDOS.) 1907 SB
225 1589 1769 (Reboot CP/M by using the warm start procedure, CTRL-C, or by performing a cold start) 1769 SB
225 1648 1931 (whenever the disks are changed. If a changed disk is to be read but not written, BDOS allows the) 1931 SB
225 1707 1891 (disk to be changed without the warm or cold start, but internally marks the drive as Read-Only.) 1891 SB
225 1766 1918 (The status of the drive is subsequently changed to Read-Write if a warm or cold start occurs. On) 1918 SB
225 1826 1943 (issuing this message, CP/M waits for input from the console. An automatic warm start takes place) 1943 SB
225 1885 397 (following any input.) 397 SB
