225 227 761 (1.8 Operation of CP/M on the MDS) 761 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 345 1786 (This section gives operating procedures for using CP/M on the Intel MDS microcomputer) 1786 SB
225 405 1888 (development system. Basic knowledge of the MDS hardware and software systems is assumed.) 1888 SB
225 523 1825 (CP/M is initiated in essentially the same manner as the Intel ISIS operating system. The disk) 1825 SB
225 582 1755 (drives are labeled 0 through 3 on the MDS, corresponding to CP/M drives A through D,) 1755 SB
225 641 1919 (respectively. The CP/M system disk is inserted into drive 0, and the BOOT and RESET switches) 1919 SB
225 700 1856 (are pressed in sequence. The interrupt 2 light should go on at this point. The space bar is then) 1856 SB
225 760 1893 (pressed on the system console, and the light should go out. If it does not, the user should check) 1893 SB
225 819 1826 (connections and baud rates. The BOOT switch is turned off, and the CP/M sign-on message) 1826 SB
225 878 1885 (should appear at the selected console device, followed by the A> system prompt. You can then) 1885 SB
225 937 1003 (issue the various resident and transient commands.) 1003 SB
225 1055 1889 (The CP/M system can be restarted \(warm start\) at any time by pushing the INT 0 switch on the) 1889 SB
225 1115 1904 (front panel. The built-in Intel ROM monitor can be initiated by pushing the INT 7 switch, which) 1904 SB
225 1174 1865 (generates an RST 7, except when operating under DDT, in which case the DDT program gets) 1865 SB
225 1233 307 (control instead.) 307 SB
225 1351 1876 (Diskettes can be removed from the drives at any time, and the system can be shut down during) 1876 SB
225 1410 1813 (operation without affecting data integrity. Do not remove a disk and replace it with another) 1813 SB
225 1470 1748 (without rebooting the system \(cold or warm start\) unless the inserted disk is Read-Only.) 1748 SB
225 1588 1825 (As a result of hardware hang-ups or malfunctions, CP/M might print the following message:) 1825 SB
225 1706 702 (BDDS ERR ON d: BAD SECTOR) 702 SB
225 1825 1944 (where d is the drive that has a permanent error. This error can occur when drive doors are opened) 1944 SB
225 1884 1931 (and closed randomly, followed by disk operations, or can be caused by a disk, drive, or controller) 1931 SB
225 1943 1936 (failure. You can optionally elect to ignore the error by pressing a single return at the console. The) 1936 SB
225 2002 1896 (error might produce a bad data record, requiring reinitialization of up to 128 bytes of data. You) 1896 SB
225 2061 1124 (can reboot the CP/M system and try the operation again.) 1124 SB
225 2180 1880 (Termination of a CP/M session requires no special action, except that it is necessary to remove) 1880 SB
225 2239 1940 (the disks before turning the power off to avoid random transients that often make their way to the) 1940 SB
225 2298 339 (drive electronics.) 339 SB
225 92 719 (1.8 Operation of CP/M on the MDS) 719 SB
1526 92 649 (CP/M Operating System Manual) 649 SB
1154 2942 92 (1-46) 92 SB
