0 0 0 fC
225 227 1908 (You should use IBM-compatible disks rather than disks that have previously been used with any) 1908 SB
225 286 1934 (ISIS version. In particular, the ISIS FORMAT operation produces nonstandard sector numbering) 1934 SB
225 345 1894 (throughout the disk. This nonstandard numbering seriously degrades the performance of CP/M,) 1894 SB
225 405 1772 (and causes CP/M to operate noticeably slower than the distribution version. If it becomes) 1772 SB
225 464 1890 (necessary to reformat a disk, which should not be the case for standard disks, a program can be) 1890 SB
225 523 1802 (written under CP/M that causes the MDS 800 controller to reformat with sequential sector) 1802 SB
225 582 642 (numbering \(1-26\) on each track.) 642 SB
225 700 1911 (Generally, IBM-compatible 8-inch disks do not need to be formatted. However, 5 1/4-inch disks) 1911 SB
225 760 426 (need to be formatted.) 426 SB
