1013 286 375 (The CP/M Editor) 375 SB
225 464 485 (2.1 Introduction to ED) 485 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 523 13 ( ) 13 SB
225 582 1942 (ED is the context editor for CP/M, and is used to create and alter CP/M source files. To start ED,) 1942 SB
225 641 777 (type a command of the following form:) 777 SB
225 760 246 (ED filename) 246 SB
225 878 43 (or) 43 SB
225 996 322 (ED filename.typ) 322 SB
225 1115 1924 (Generally, ED reads segments of the source file given by filename or filename.typ into the central) 1924 SB
225 1174 1930 (memory, where you edit the file and it is subsequently written back to disk after alterations. If the) 1930 SB
225 1233 1902 (source file does not exist before editing, it is created by ED and initialized to empty. The overall) 1902 SB
225 1292 792 (operation of ED is shown in Figure 2-1.) 792 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c356 font
225 1410 415 (2.1.1 ED Operation) 415 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 1529 1799 (ED operates upon the source file, shown in Figure 2-1 by x.y, and passes all text through a) 1799 SB
225 1588 1738 (memory buffer where the text can be viewed or altered. The number of lines that can be) 1738 SB
225 1647 1939 (maintained in the memory buffer varies with the line length, but has a total capacity of about 5000) 1939 SB
225 1706 677 (characters in a 20K CP/M system.) 677 SB
225 1825 1934 (Edited text material is written into a temporary work file under your command. Upon termination) 1934 SB
225 1884 1944 (of the edit, the memory buffer is written to the temporary file, followed by any remaining \(unread\)) 1944 SB
225 1943 1943 (text in the source file. The name of the original file is changed from x.y to x.BAK so that the most) 1943 SB
225 2002 1845 (recent edited source file can be reclaimed if necessary. See the CP/M commands ERASE and) 1845 SB
225 2061 1870 (RENAME. The temporary file is then changed from x.$$$ to x.y, which becomes the resulting) 1870 SB
225 2120 208 (edited file.) 208 SB
1166 2942 67 (2-1) 67 SB
