225 227 96 (     E) 96 SB
525 227 1588 (Ends the edit. Copy all buffered text to temporary file and copy all unprocessed ) 1588 SB
525 286 870 (source lines to temporary file. Rename files.) 870 SB
225 405 101 (     H) 101 SB
525 405 1603 (Moves to head of new file by performing automatic E command. The temporary ) 1603 SB
525 464 1481 (file becomes the new source file, the memory buffer is emptied, and a new ) 1481 SB
525 523 1505 (temporary file is created. The effect is equivalent to issuing an E command, ) 1505 SB
525 582 1222 (followed by a reinvocation of ED, using x.y as the file to edit.) 1222 SB
225 700 101 (     O) 101 SB
525 700 1505 (Returns to original file. The memory buffer is emptied, the temporary file is ) 1505 SB
525 760 1604 (deleted, and the SP is returned to position 1 of the source file. The effects of the ) 1604 SB
525 819 898 (previous editing commands are thus nullified.) 898 SB
225 937 101 (     Q) 101 SB
525 937 1014 (Quits edit with no file alterations, returns to CP/M.) 1014 SB
225 1055 1884 (There are a number of special cases to consider. If the integer n is omitted in any ED command) 1884 SB
225 1115 1869 (where an integer is allowed, then 1 is assumed. Thus, the commands A and W append one line) 1869 SB
225 1174 1892 (and write one line, respectively. In addition, if a pound sign # is given in the place of n, then the) 1892 SB
225 1233 1900 (integer 65535 is assumed \(the largest value for n that is allowed\). Because most source files can) 1900 SB
225 1292 1883 (be contained entirely in the memory buffer, the command #A is often issued at the beginning of) 1883 SB
225 1351 1858 (the edit to read the entire source file to memory. Similarly, the command #W writes the entire) 1858 SB
225 1410 550 (buffer to the temporary file.) 550 SB
225 1529 1913 (Two special forms of the A and W commands are provided as a convenience. The command OA) 1913 SB
225 1588 1887 (fills the current memory buffer at least half full, while OW writes lines until the buffer is at least) 1887 SB
225 1647 1820 (half empty. An error is issued if the memory buffer size is exceeded. You can then enter any) 1820 SB
225 1706 1913 (command, such as W, that does not increase memory requirements. The remainder of any partial) 1913 SB
225 1765 1770 (line read during the overflow will be brought into memory on the next successful append.) 1770 SB
