225 227 1940 (You can reference an absolute line number by preceding any command by a number followed by a) 1940 SB
225 286 1840 (colon, in the same format as the line number display. In this case, the ED program moves the) 1840 SB
225 345 1903 (current line reference to the absolute line number, if the line exists in the current memory buffer.) 1903 SB
225 405 1937 (The line denoted by the absolute line number must be in the memory buffer \(see the A command\).) 1937 SB
225 464 392 (Thus, the command) 392 SB
225 582 120 (345:T) 120 SB
225 700 1134 (is interpreted as move to absolute 345, and type the line. ) 1134 SB
225 760 1177 (Absolute line numbers are produced only during the editing) 1177 SB
225 819 1179 (process and are not recorded with the file. In particular, the) 1179 SB
225 878 1291 (line numbers will change following a deleted or expanded section) 1291 SB
225 937 143 (of text.) 143 SB
225 1055 1829 ( You can also reference an absolute line number as a backward or forward distance from the) 1829 SB
225 1115 1542 (current line by preceding the absolute number by a colon. Thus, the command) 1542 SB
225 1233 120 (:400T) 120 SB
225 1351 1945 (is interpreted as type from the current line number through the line whose absolute number is 400.) 1945 SB
225 1410 1093 (Combining the two line reference forms, the command ) 1093 SB
225 1529 209 (345::400T) 209 SB
225 1647 1853 (is interpreted as move to absolute line 345, then type through absolute line 400. Absolute line) 1853 SB
225 1706 1388 (references of this sort can precede any of the standard ED commands.) 1388 SB
225 1825 1901 (Line numbering is controlled by the V \(Verify Line Numbers\) command. Line numbering can be) 1901 SB
225 1884 753 (turned off by typing the -V command.) 753 SB
225 2002 1340 (If the file to edit does not exist, ED displays the following message:) 1340 SB
225 2120 231 (NEW FILE) 231 SB
225 2239 1926 (To move text into the memory buffer, you must enter an i command before typing input lines and) 1926 SB
225 2298 1875 (terminate each line with a carriage return. A single CTRL-Z character returns ED to command) 1875 SB
225 2357 123 (mode.) 123 SB
