225 227 678 (2.1.5 Memory Buffer Operation) 678 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 345 1884 (When ED begins, the memory buffer is empty. You can either append lines from the source file) 1884 SB
225 405 1898 (with the A command, or enter the lines directly from the console with the insert command.  The) 1898 SB
225 464 828 (insert command takes the following form:) 828 SB
225 582 17 (I) 17 SB
225 700 1938 (ED then accepts any number of input lines. You must terminate each line with a <cr> \(the <If > is) 1938 SB
225 760 1946 (supplied automatically\). A single CTRL-Z, denoted by an up arrow \(T\)Z, returns ED to command) 1946 SB
225 819 1677 (mode. The CP is positioned after the last character entered. The following sequence:) 1677 SB
225 937 125 (I <cr>) 125 SB
225 996 382 (NOW IS THE<cr>) 382 SB
225 1055 327 (TIME FOR<cr>) 327 SB
225 1115 471 (ALL GOOD MEN<cr>) 471 SB
225 1174 53 (^Z) 53 SB
225 1292 555 (leaves the memory buffer as) 555 SB
225 1410 470 (NOW IS THE<cr><If>) 470 SB
225 1470 415 (TIME FOR<cr><If>) 415 SB
225 1529 572 (ALL GOOD MEN<cr> <If>) 572 SB
225 1647 1898 (Generally, ED accepts command letters in upper- or lower-case.  If the command is upper-case,) 1898 SB
225 1706 1869 (all input values associated with the command are translated to upper-case. If the I command is) 1869 SB
225 1765 1928 (typed, all input lines are automatically translated internally to upper-case. The lower-case form of) 1928 SB
225 1825 1819 (the i command is most often used to allow both upper- and lower-case letters to be entered.) 1819 SB
225 1943 1897 (Various commands can be issued that control the CP or display source text in the vicinity of the) 1897 SB
225 2002 1921 (CP. The commands shown below with a preceding n indicate that an optional unsigned value can) 1921 SB
225 2061 1923 (be specified. When preceded by +-, the command can be unsigned, or have an optional preceding) 1923 SB
225 2120 1893 (plus or minus sign. As before, the pound sign # is replaced by 65535. If an integer n is optional,) 1893 SB
225 2180 1940 (but not supplied, then n=1 is assumed. Finally, if a plus sign is optional, but none is specified, then) 1940 SB
225 2239 267 (+ is assumed.) 267 SB
225 92 458 (2.1 Introduction to ED) 458 SB
