225 227 818 (                Table 2-2.  Editing Commands) 818 SB
225 345 65 (     ) 65 SB
32 0 0 50 50 1 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
290 345 442 (Command        Action) 442 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 464 143 (     +-B) 143 SB
525 464 1224 (Move CP to beginning of memory buffer if + and to bottom if) 1224 SB
225 582 167 (     +-nC) 167 SB
525 582 1572 (Move CP by +-n characters \(moving ahead if +\), counting the <cr><lf> as two ) 1572 SB
525 641 215 (characters.) 215 SB
225 760 170 (     +-nD) 170 SB
525 760 1256 (Delete n characters ahead of CP if plus and behind CP if minus.) 1256 SB
225 878 169 (     +-nK) 169 SB
525 878 1597 (Kill \(remove\) +-n lines of source text using CP as the current reference. If CP is ) 1597 SB
525 937 1634 (not at the beginning of the current line when K is issued, the characters before CP ) 1634 SB
525 996 1562 (remain if + is specified, while the characters after CP remain if - is given in the ) 1562 SB
525 1055 206 (command.) 206 SB
225 1174 164 (     +-nL) 164 SB
525 1174 1648 (If n = 0, move CP to the beginning of the current line, if it is not already there. If n ) 1648 SB
525 1233 1639 (<> 0, first move the CP to the beginning of the current line and then move it to the) 1639 SB
525 1292 1634 (beginning of the line that is n lines down \(if +\) or up \(if -\). The CP will stop at the ) 1634 SB
525 1351 1431 (top or bottom of the memory buffer if too large a value of n is specified.) 1431 SB
225 1470 165 (     +-nT) 165 SB
525 1470 1622 (If n = 0, type the contents of the current line up to CP. If n = 1, type the contents ) 1622 SB
525 1529 1542 (of the current line from CP to the end of the line. If n>1, type the current line ) 1542 SB
525 1588 1646 (along with n +- 1 lines that follow, if + is specified. Similarly, if n>1 and - is given, ) 1646 SB
525 1647 1570 (type the previous n lines up to the CP. Any key can be depressed to abort long ) 1570 SB
525 1706 200 (type-outs.) 200 SB
225 1825 134 (     +-n) 134 SB
525 1825 1396 (Equivalent to +-nLT, which moves up or down and types a single line.) 1396 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c356 font
225 1943 503 (2.1.6 Command Strings) 503 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 2061 1877 (Any number of commands can be typed contiguously \(up to the capacity of the console buffer\)) 1877 SB
225 2120 1753 (and are executed only after you press the <cr>. Table 2-3 summarizes the CP/M console) 1753 SB
225 2180 1250 (line-editing commands used to control the input command line.) 1250 SB
