225 1647 1929 (where s represents the string to match, followed by either a <cr> or CTRL-Z, denoted by ^Z. ED) 1929 SB
225 1706 1867 (starts at the current position of CP and attempts to match the string. The match is attempted n) 1867 SB
225 1765 1766 (times and, if successful, the CP is moved directly after the string. If the n matches are not) 1766 SB
225 1825 1832 (successful, the CP is not moved from its initial position. Search strings can include CTRL-L,) 1832 SB
225 1884 996 (which is replaced by the pair of symbols <cr><lf>.) 996 SB
