225 227 1855 (where filename is the primary filename of a source file on the disk with an assumed filetype of) 1855 SB
225 286 1892 (LIB. ED reads the specified file, and places the characters into the memory buffer after CP, in a) 1892 SB
225 345 1125 (manner similar to the I command. Thus, if the command ) 1125 SB
225 464 309 (RMACRO<cr>) 309 SB
225 582 1716 (is issued by the operator, ED reads from the file MACRO.LIB until the end-of-file and) 1716 SB
225 641 1178 (automatically inserts the characters into the memory buffer.) 1178 SB
225 760 1947 (ED also includes a block move facility implemented through the X \(Transfer\) command. The form) 1947 SB
375 878 60 (nX) 60 SB
225 996 1409 (transfers the next n lines from the current line to a temporary file called) 1409 SB
225 1115 279 (X$$$$$$.LIB) 279 SB
225 1233 1883 (which is active only during the editing process. You can reposition the current line reference to) 1883 SB
225 1292 1775 (any portion of the source file and transfer lines to the temporary file. The transferred lines) 1775 SB
225 1351 1546 (accumulate one after another in this file and can be retrieved by simply typing ) 1546 SB
225 1470 33 (R) 33 SB
225 1588 1947 (which is the trivial case of the library read command. In this case, the entire transferred set of lines) 1947 SB
225 1647 1891 (is read into the memory buffer. Note that the X command does not remove the transferred lines) 1891 SB
225 1706 1812 (from the memory buffer, although a K command can be used directly after the X, and the R) 1812 SB
225 1765 1807 (command does not empty the transferred LIB file. That is, given that a set of lines has been) 1807 SB
225 1825 1949 (transferred with the X command, they can be reread any number of times back into the source file.) 1949 SB
225 1884 283 (The command) 283 SB
225 2002 61 (0X) 61 SB
225 2120 881 (is provided to empty the transferred line file.) 881 SB
225 2239 1909 (Note that upon normal completion of the ED program through Q or E, the temporary LIB file is) 1909 SB
225 2298 1881 (removed. If ED is aborted with a CTRL-C, the LIB file will exist if lines have been transferred,) 1881 SB
225 2357 1715 (but will generally be empty \(a subsequent ED invocation will erase the temporary file\).) 1715 SB
