225 345 1902 (A label is an identifier that occurs on a particular statement. In general, the label is given a value) 1902 SB
225 405 1799 (determined by the type of statement that it precedes. If the label occurs on a statement that) 1799 SB
225 464 1835 (generates machine code or reserves memory space \(for example, a MOV instruction or a DS) 1835 SB
225 523 1884 (pseudo operation\), the label is given the value of the program address that it labels.  If the label) 1884 SB
225 582 1859 (precedes an EQU or SET, the label is given the value that results from evaluating the operand) 1859 SB
225 641 1550 (field. Except for the SET statement, an identifier can label only one statement.) 1550 SB
