225 227 524 (3.4.3 The EQU Directive) 524 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 345 1918 (The EQU \(equate\) statement is used to set up synonyms for particular numeric values. The EQU) 1918 SB
225 405 503 (statement takes the form:) 503 SB
375 523 431 (label EQU expression) 431 SB
225 641 1910 (where the label must be present and must not label any other statement. The assembler evaluates) 1910 SB
225 700 1822 (the expression and assigns this value to the identifier given in the label field. The identifier is) 1822 SB
225 760 1881 (usually a name that describes the value in a more human-oriented manner. Further, this name is) 1881 SB
225 819 1860 (used throughout the program to place parameters on certain functions. Suppose data received) 1860 SB
225 878 1943 (from a teletype appears on a particular input port, and data is sent to the teletype through the next) 1943 SB
225 937 1933 (output port in sequence. For example, you can use this series of equate statements to define these) 1933 SB
225 996 882 (ports for a particular hardware environment:) 882 SB
225 1115 264 (TTYBASE   ) 264 SB
525 1115 306 (EQU 10H        ) 306 SB
1125 1115 727 (;BASE PORT NUMBER FOR TTY) 727 SB
225 1174 216 (TTYIN     ) 216 SB
525 1174 393 (EQU TTYBASE    ) 393 SB
1125 1174 327 (;TTY DATA IN) 327 SB
225 1233 253 (TTYOUT    ) 253 SB
525 1233 420 (EQU TTYBASE+1  ) 420 SB
1125 1233 377 (;TTY DATA OUT) 377 SB
225 1351 1841 (At a later point in the program, the statements that access the teletype can appear as follows:) 1841 SB
225 1470 79 (IN  ) 79 SB
525 1470 229 (TTYIN      ) 229 SB
1125 1470 654 (;READ TTY DATA TO REG-A) 654 SB
225 1588 91 (   ....) 91 SB
225 1706 116 (OUT ) 116 SB
525 1706 266 (TTYOUT     ) 266 SB
1125 1706 830 (;WRITE DATA TO TTY FROM REG-A) 830 SB
225 1825 1758 (making the program more readable than if the absolute I/O ports are used. Further, if the) 1758 SB
225 1884 1892 (hardware environment is redefined to start the teletype communications ports at 7FH instead of) 1892 SB
225 1943 962 (10H, the first statement need only be changed to) 962 SB
225 2061 238 (TTYBASE ) 238 SB
525 2061 243 (EQU 7FH   ) 243 SB
1125 2061 740 (;BASE PORT NUMBER FOR TTY ) 740 SB
225 2180 1513 (and the program can be reassembled without changing any other statements.) 1513 SB
225 92 497 (3.4 Assembler Directives) 497 SB
1526 92 649 (CP/M Operating System Manual) 649 SB
