225 227 510 (3.4.4 The SET Directive) 510 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 345 1161 (The SET statement is similar to the EQU, taking the form:) 1161 SB
375 464 418 (label SET expression) 418 SB
225 582 1872 (except that the label can occur on other SET statements within the program. The expression is) 1872 SB
225 641 1833 (evaluated and becomes the current value associated with the label. Thus, the EQU statement) 1833 SB
225 700 1900 (defines a label with a single value, while the SET statement defines a value that is valid from the) 1900 SB
225 760 1927 (current SET statement to the point where the label occurs on the next SET statement. The use of) 1927 SB
225 819 1773 (the SET is similar to the EQU statement, but is used most often in controlling conditional) 1773 SB
225 878 191 (assembly.) 191 SB
