225 227 1926 (When encountering the IF statement, the assembler evaluates the expression following the IF. All) 1926 SB
225 286 1920 (operands in the expression must be defined ahead of the IF statement. If the expression evaluates) 1920 SB
225 345 1786 (to a nonzero value, then statement#l through statement#n are assembled. If the expression) 1786 SB
225 405 1933 (evaluates to zero, the statements are listed but not assembled.  Conditional assembly is often used) 1933 SB
225 464 1917 (to write a single generic program that includes a number of possible run-time environments, with) 1917 SB
225 523 1877 (only a few specific portions of the program selected for any particular assembly. The following) 1877 SB
225 582 1832 (program segments, for example, might be part of a program that communicates with either a) 1832 SB
225 641 1808 (teletype or a CRT console \(but not both\) by selecting a particular value for TTY before the) 1808 SB
225 700 330 (assembly begins.) 330 SB
