225 227 486 (3.4.6 The DB Directive) 486 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 345 1931 (The DB directive allows the programmer to define initialized storage areas in singleprecision byte) 1931 SB
225 405 833 (format. The DB statement takes the form:) 833 SB
375 523 532 (label DB e#1, e#2, ... , e#n) 532 SB
225 641 1932 (where e#1 through e#n are either expressions that evaluate to 8-bit values \(the highorder bit must) 1932 SB
225 700 1792 (be zero\) or are ASCII strings of length no greater than 64 characters. There is no practical) 1792 SB
225 760 1847 (restriction on the number of expressions included on a single source line. The expressions are) 1847 SB
225 819 1882 (evaluated and placed sequentially into the machine code file following the last program address) 1882 SB
225 878 1892 (generated by the assembler. String characters are similarly placed into memory starting with the) 1892 SB
225 937 1865 (first character and ending with the last character. Strings of length greater than two characters) 1865 SB
225 996 1215 (cannot be used as operands in more complicated expressions.) 1215 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c356 font
225 1115 117 (Note:) 117 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
342 1116 1827 (ASCII characters are always placed in memory with the parity bit reset \(0\). Also, there is no) 1827 SB
225 1175 1899 (translation from lower- to upper-case within strings. The optional label can be used to reference) 1899 SB
225 1234 1902 (the data area throughout the remainder of the program. The following are examples of valid DB) 1902 SB
225 1293 224 (statements:) 224 SB
375 1411 137 (data:   ) 137 SB
675 1411 95 (DB  ) 95 SB
825 1411 215 (0,1,2,3,4,5) 215 SB
225 1471 130 (          ) 130 SB
675 1471 95 (DB  ) 95 SB
825 1471 619 (data and 0ffh,5,377Q,1+2+3+4) 619 SB
375 1530 187 (sign-on:  ) 187 SB
675 1530 95 (DB  ) 95 SB
825 1530 645 ('please type your name',CR,LF,0) 645 SB
225 1589 195 (               ) 195 SB
675 1589 95 (DB  ) 95 SB
825 1589 611 ('AB' SHR 8,'C','DE',AND 7FH) 611 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c356 font
225 1707 502 (3.4.7 The DW Directive) 502 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 1826 1845 (The DW statement is similar to the DB statement except double-precision two-byte words of) 1845 SB
225 1885 1137 (storage are initialized. The DW statement takes the form:) 1137 SB
375 2003 532 (label DW e#1, e#2, ..., e#n) 532 SB
225 2121 1923 (where e#1 through e#n are expressions that evaluate to 16-bit results. Note that ASCII strings of) 1923 SB
225 2181 1888 (one or two characters are allowed, but strings longer than two characters are disallowed.  In all) 1888 SB
225 2240 1825 (cases, the data storage is consistent with the 8080 processor; the least significant byte of the) 1825 SB
225 2299 1853 (expression is stored first in memory, followed by the most significant byte.  The following are) 1853 SB
225 2358 569 (examples of DW statements:) 569 SB
375 2476 127 (doub: ) 127 SB
675 2476 753 (DW 0ffefh,doub+4,signon-$,255+255) 753 SB
225 2536 78 (      ) 78 SB
675 2536 618 (DW 'a',5,'ab','CD',6 shl 8 or llb.) 618 SB
