225 996 438 (3.5 Operation Codes) 438 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 1115 1896 (Assembly-language operation codes form the principal part of assembly-language programs and) 1896 SB
225 1174 1890 (form the operation field of the instruction. In general, ASM accepts all the standard mnemonics) 1890 SB
225 1233 1923 (for the Intel 8080 microcomputer, which are given in detail in the Intel 8080 Assembly Language) 1923 SB
225 1292 1902 (Programming Manual. Labels are optional on each input line. The individual operators are listed) 1902 SB
225 1351 1944 (briefly in the following sections for completeness, although the Intel manuals should be referenced) 1944 SB
225 1410 1825 (for exact operator details. In Tables 3-4 through 3-8, bit values have the following meaning:) 1825 SB
225 1529 116 (   -e3 ) 116 SB
375 1529 1765 (represents a 3-bit value in the range 0-7 that can be one of the predefined registers A, B, ) 1765 SB
375 1588 619 (C, D, E, H, L, M, SP, or PSW.) 619 SB
225 1706 103 (   -e8) 103 SB
375 1706 874 (represents an 8-bit value in the range 0-255.) 874 SB
225 1825 1066 (   -e16 represents a 16-bit value in the range 0-65535.) 1066 SB
225 1943 1861 (These expressions can be formed from an arbitrary combination of operands and operators. In) 1861 SB
225 2002 1945 (some cases, the operands are restricted to particular values within the allowable range, such as the) 1945 SB
225 2061 1307 (PUSH instruction. These cases are noted as they are encountered.) 1307 SB
225 2180 1857 (In the sections that follow, each operation code is listed in its most general form, along with a) 1857 SB
225 2239 1219 (specific example, a short explanation, and special restrictions.) 1219 SB
