225 1174 733 (4.2.1 The A \(Assembly\) Command) 733 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 1292 1907 (DDT allows in-line assembly language to be inserted into the current memory image using the A) 1907 SB
225 1351 649 (command, which takes the form:) 649 SB
225 1470 54 (As) 54 SB
225 1588 1868 (where s is the hexadecimal starting address for the in-line assembly. DDT prompts the console) 1868 SB
225 1647 1578 (with the address of the next instruction to fill and reads the console, looking for) 1578 SB
225 1706 1736 (assembly-language mnemonics followed by register references and operands in absolute) 1736 SB
225 1765 1705 (hexadecimal form. See the Intel 8080 Assembly Language Reference Card for a list of) 1705 SB
225 1825 1931 (mnemonics. Each successive load address is printed before reading the console.  The A command) 1931 SB
225 1884 1224 (terminates when the first empty line is input from the console.) 1224 SB
225 2002 1839 (Upon completion of assembly language input, you can review the memory segment using the) 1839 SB
225 2061 812 (DDT disassembler \(see the L command\).) 812 SB
225 2180 1873 (Note that the assembler/disassembler portion of DDT can be overlaid by the transient program) 1873 SB
225 2239 1929 (being tested, in which case the DDT program responds with an error condition when the A and L) 1929 SB
225 2298 403 (commands are used.) 403 SB
225 92 415 (4.2 DDT Commands) 415 SB
