225 227 690 (4.2.2 The D \(Display\) Command) 690 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 345 1913 (The D command allows you to view the contents of memory in hexadecimal and ASCII formats.) 1913 SB
225 405 663 (The D command takes the forms:) 663 SB
375 523 36 (D) 36 SB
375 582 55 (Ds) 55 SB
375 641 83 (Ds,f) 83 SB
225 760 1785 (In the first form, memory is displayed from the current display address, initially 100H, and) 1785 SB
225 819 1449 (continues for 16 display lines.  Each display line takes the followng form:) 1449 SB
225 937 1520 (     aaaa bb bb bb bb bb bb bb bb bb bb bb bb bb bb bb bb   cccccccccccccccc) 1520 SB
225 1055 1797 (where aaaa is the display address in hexadecimal and bb represents data present in memory) 1797 SB
