225 2298 109 (Fs,f,c) 109 SB
225 2416 1888 (where s is the starting address, f is the final address, and c is a hexadecimal byte constant. DDT) 1888 SB
225 2475 1891 (stores the constant c at address s, increments the value of s and test against f. If s exceeds f, the) 1891 SB
225 2535 1909 (operation terminates, otherwise the operation is repeated. Thus, the fill command can be used to) 1909 SB
225 2594 950 (set a memory block to a specific constant value.) 950 SB
