32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 345 1924 (A program is executed using the G command, with up to two optional breakpoint addresses. The) 1924 SB
225 405 573 (G command takes the forms:) 573 SB
375 523 36 (G) 36 SB
375 582 55 (Gs) 55 SB
375 641 92 (Gs,b) 92 SB
375 700 127 (Gs,b,c) 127 SB
375 760 73 (G,b) 73 SB
375 819 108 (G,b,c) 108 SB
225 937 1865 (The first form executes the program at the current value of the program counter in the current) 1865 SB
225 996 1915 (machine state, with no breakpoints set. The only way to regain control in DDT is through a RST) 1915 SB
225 1055 1785 (7 execution. The current program counter can be viewed by typing an X or XP command.) 1785 SB
225 1174 1862 (The second form is similar to the first, except that the program counter in the current machine) 1862 SB
225 1233 950 (state is set to address s before execution begins.) 950 SB
225 1351 1912 (The third form is the same as the second, except that program execution stops when address b is) 1912 SB
225 1410 1930 (encountered \(b must be in the area of the program under test\). The instruction at location b is not) 1930 SB
225 1470 909 (executed when the breakpoint is encountered.) 909 SB
225 1588 1886 (The fourth form is identical to the third, except that two breakpoints are specified, one at b and) 1886 SB
225 1647 1909 (the other at c. Encountering either breakpoint causes execution to stop and both breakpoints are) 1909 SB
225 1706 1917 (cleared. The last two forms take the program counter from the current machine state and set one) 1917 SB
225 1765 679 (and two breakpoints, respectively.) 679 SB
225 1884 1847 (Execution continues from the starting address in real-time to the next breakpoint. There is no) 1847 SB
225 1943 1872 (intervention between the starting address and the break address by DDT. If the program under) 1872 SB
225 2002 1799 (test does not reach a breakpoint, control cannot return to DDT without executing a RST 7) 1799 SB
225 2061 1531 (instruction. Upon encountering a breakpoint, DDT stops execution and types) 1531 SB
