225 2298 1880 (disassembled code from s through address f. In all three cases, the list address is set to the next) 1880 SB
225 2357 1875 (unlisted location in preparation for a subsequent L command. Upon encountering an execution) 1875 SB
225 2416 1714 (breakpoint, the list address is set to the current value of the program counter \(G and T) 1714 SB
225 2475 1884 (commands\). Again, long typeouts can be aborted by pressing RETURN during the list process.) 1884 SB
