32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 996 1935 (The R command is used in conjunction with the I command to read COM and HEX files from the) 1935 SB
225 1055 1898 (disk into the transient program area in preparation for the debug run. The R command takes the) 1898 SB
225 1115 128 (forms:) 128 SB
375 1233 33 (R) 33 SB
375 1292 57 (Rb) 57 SB
225 1410 1908 (where b is an optional bias address that is added to each program or data address as It is loaded.) 1908 SB
225 1470 1886 (The load operation must not overwrite any of the system parameters from 000H through 0FFH) 1886 SB
225 1529 1855 (\(that is, the first page of memory\). If b is omitted, then b = 0000 is assumed. The R command) 1855 SB
225 1588 1938 (requires a previous I command, specifying the name of a HEX or COM file.  The load address for) 1938 SB
225 1647 1945 (each record is obtained from each individual HEX record, while an assumed load address of 100H) 1945 SB
225 1706 1788 (is used for COM files. Note that any number of R commands can be issued following the I) 1788 SB
225 1765 1864 (command to reread the program under test, assuming the tested program does not destroy the) 1864 SB
225 1825 1939 (default area at 5CH. Any file specified with the filetype COM is assumed to contain machine code) 1939 SB
225 1884 1904 (in pure binary form \(created with the LOAD or SAVE command\), and all others are assumed to) 1904 SB
225 1943 1830 (contain machine code in Intel hex format \(produced, for example, with the ASM command\).) 1830 SB
