32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 1706 1940 (The T command allows selective tracing of program execution for 1 to 65535 program steps. The) 1940 SB
225 1765 568 (T command takes the forms:) 568 SB
375 1884 31 (T) 31 SB
375 1943 55 (Tn) 55 SB
225 2061 1910 (In the first form, the CPU state is displayed and the next program step is executed. The program) 1910 SB
225 2120 1297 (terminates immediately, with the termination address displayed as) 1297 SB
375 2239 121 (*hhhh) 121 SB
225 2357 1926 (where hhhh is the next address to execute. The display address \(used in the D command\) is set to) 1926 SB
225 2416 1918 (the value of H and L, and the list address \(used in the L command\) is set to hhhh. The CPU state) 1918 SB
225 2475 1357 (at program termination can then be examined using the X command.) 1357 SB
