225 227 840 (5.2 Operating System Call Conventions) 840 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 345 1916 (This section provides detailed information for performing direct operating system calls from user) 1916 SB
225 405 1950 (programs. Many of the functions listed below, however, are accessed more simply through the I/O) 1950 SB
225 464 1917 (macro library provided with the MAC macro assembler and listed in the Digital Research manual) 1917 SB
225 523 1666 (entitled, "Programmer's Utilities Guide for the CP/M Family of Operating Systems.") 1666 SB
225 641 1937 (CP/M facilities that are available for access by transient programs fall into two general categories:) 1937 SB
225 700 1370 (simple device I/O and disk file I/O. The simple device operations are ) 1370 SB
225 760 26 (  ) 26 SB
225 819 563 (   - read a console character ) 563 SB
225 878 579 (   - write a console character ) 579 SB
225 937 610 (   - read a sequential character ) 610 SB
225 996 626 (   - write a sequential character ) 626 SB
225 1055 477 (   - get or set I/O status ) 477 SB
225 1115 470 (   - print console buffer ) 470 SB
225 1174 572 (   - interrogate console ready) 572 SB
225 1292 999 (The following FDOS operations perform disk I/O:) 999 SB
