225 1351 1943 (CP/M implements a named file structure on each disk, providing a logical organization that allows) 1943 SB
225 1410 1924 (any particular file to contain any number of records from completely emptv to the full capacity of) 1924 SB
225 1470 1761 (the drive. Each drive is logically distinct with a disk directory and file data area. The disk) 1761 SB
225 1529 1764 (filenames are in three parts: the drive select code, the filename \(consisting of one to eight) 1764 SB
225 1588 1821 (nonblank characters\), and the filetype \(consisting of zero to three nonblank characters\). The) 1821 SB
225 1647 1921 (filetype names the generic category of a particular file, while the filename distinguishes individual) 1921 SB
225 1706 1874 (files in each category. The filetypes listed in Table 5-1 name a few generic categories that have) 1874 SB
225 1765 1100 (been established, although they are somewhat arbitrary.) 1100 SB
