225 819 1831 (The Select Disk function designates the disk drive named in register E as the default disk for) 1831 SB
225 878 1727 (subsequent file operations, with E = 0 for drive A, 1 for drive B, and so on through 15,) 1727 SB
225 937 1908 (corresponding to drive P in a full 16 drive system. The drive is placed in an on-line status, which) 1908 SB
225 996 1888 (activates its directory until the next cold start, warm start, or disk system reset operation. If the) 1888 SB
225 1055 1937 (disk medium is changed while it is on-line, the drive automatically goes to a Read-Only status in a) 1937 SB
225 1115 1829 (standard CP/M environment, see Function 28. FCBs that specify drive code zero \(dr = 00H\)) 1829 SB
225 1174 1896 (automatically reference the currently selected default drive. Drive code values between I and 16) 1896 SB
225 1233 1478 (ignore the selected default drive and directly reference drives A through P.) 1478 SB
