225 1884 1868 (The Read Random function is similar to the sequential file read operation of previous releases,) 1868 SB
225 1943 1867 (except that the read operation takes place at a particular record number, selected by the 24-bit) 1867 SB
225 2002 1902 (value constructed from the 3-byte field following the FCB \(byte positions r0 at 33, r1 at 34, and) 1902 SB
225 2061 1868 (r2 at 35\). The user should note that the sequence of 24 bits is stored with least significant byte) 1868 SB
225 2120 1904 (first \(r0\), middle byte next \(r1\), and high byte last \(r2\). CP/M does not reference byte r2, except) 1904 SB
225 2180 1843 (in computing the size of a file \(Function 35\). Byte r2 must be zero, however, since a nonzero) 1843 SB
225 2239 875 (value indicates overflow past the end of file.) 875 SB
