225 1055 1869 (The Write Random operation is initiated similarly to the Read Random call, except that data is) 1869 SB
225 1115 1927 (written to the disk from the current DMA address. Further, if the disk extent or data block that is) 1927 SB
225 1174 1842 (the target of the write has not yet been allocated, the allocation is performed before the write) 1842 SB
225 1233 1781 (operation continues.  As in the Read Random operation, the random record number is not) 1781 SB
225 1292 1863 (changed as a result of the write. The logical extent number and current record positions of the) 1863 SB
225 1351 1890 (FCB are set to correspond to the random record that is being written. Again, sequential read or) 1890 SB
225 1410 1756 (write operations can begin following a random write, with the notation that the currently) 1756 SB
225 1470 1939 (addressed record is either read or rewritten again as the sequential operation begins. You can also) 1939 SB
225 1529 1900 (simply advance the random record position following each write to get the effect of a sequential) 1900 SB
225 1588 1874 (write operation. Note that reading or writing the last record of an extent in random mode does) 1874 SB
225 1647 1340 (not cause an automatic extent switch as it does in sequential mode. ) 1340 SB
225 1765 1890 (The error codes returned by a random write are identical to the random read operation with the) 1890 SB
225 1825 1811 (addition of error code 05, which indicates that a new extent cannot be created as a result of) 1811 SB
225 1884 383 (directory overflow.) 383 SB
