225 227 752 (6.2 First-level System Regeneration) 752 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 345 1840 (The procedure to patch the CP/M system is given below. Address references in each step are) 1840 SB
225 405 1907 (shown with H denoting the hexadecimal radix, and are given for a 20K CP/M system. For larger) 1907 SB
225 464 1863 (CP/M systems, a bias is added to each address that is shown with a +b following it, where b is) 1863 SB
225 523 1905 (equal to the memory size-20K. Values for b in various standard memory sizes are listed in Table) 1905 SB
225 582 80 (6-1.) 80 SB
225 700 992 (             Table 6-1. Standard Memory Size Values) 992 SB
225 819 65 (     ) 65 SB
32 0 0 50 50 1 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
290 819 435 (Memory Size    Value) 435 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 937 902 (     24K:           b = 24K - 20K = 4K = 1000H) 902 SB
225 996 927 (     32K:           b = 32K - 20K = 12K = 3000H) 927 SB
225 1055 927 (     40K:           b = 40K - 20K = 20K = 5000H) 927 SB
225 1115 927 (     48K:           b = 48K - 20K = 28K = 7000H) 927 SB
225 1174 927 (     56K:           b = 56K - 20K = 36K = 9000H) 927 SB
225 1233 937 (     62K:           b = 62K - 20K = 42K = A800H) 937 SB
225 1292 935 (     64K:           b = 64K - 20K = 44K = B000H) 935 SB
225 1410 1813 (Note that the standard distribution version of CP/M is set for operation within a 20K CP/M) 1813 SB
225 1470 1841 (system. Therefore, you must first bring up the 20K CP/M system, then configure it for actual) 1841 SB
225 1529 611 (memory size \(see Section 6.3\).) 611 SB
225 1588 13 ( ) 13 SB
225 1647 940 (Follow these steps to patch your CP/M system:) 940 SB
225 1765 64 (  1.) 64 SB
375 1765 1750 (Read Section 6.4 and write a GETSYS program that reads the first two tracks of a disk ) 1750 SB
375 1825 1685 (into memory. The program from the disk must be loaded starting at location 3380H. ) 1685 SB
375 1884 1746 (GETSYS is coded to start at location 100H \(base of the TPA\) as shown in Appendix C.) 1746 SB
225 1943 13 ( ) 13 SB
225 2002 64 (  2.) 64 SB
375 2002 1798 (Test the GETSYS program by reading a blank disk into memory, and check to see that the) 1798 SB
375 2061 1668 (data has been read properly and that the disk has not been altered in any way by the ) 1668 SB
375 2120 385 (GETSYS program.) 385 SB
225 2180 13 ( ) 13 SB
