225 1055 1942 (An image of CP/M in the TPA is configured for the requested memory size. The memory image is) 1942 SB
225 1115 1948 (at location 0900H through 227FH, that is, the BOOT is at 0900H, the CCP is at 980H, the BDOS) 1948 SB
225 1174 1777 (starts at 1180H, and the BIOS is at 1F80H. Note that the memory image has the standard) 1777 SB
225 1233 1906 (MDS-800 BIOS and BOOT on it. It is now necessary to save the memory image in a file so that) 1906 SB
225 1292 933 (you can patch the CBIOS and CBOOT into it: ) 933 SB
225 1410 485 (SAVE 34 CPMxx.COM) 485 SB
225 1529 1928 (The memory image created by the MOVCPM program is offset by a negative bias so that it loads) 1928 SB
225 1588 1874 (into the free area of the TPA, and thus does not interfere with the operation of CP/M in higher) 1874 SB
225 1647 1942 (memory. This memory image can be subsequently loaded under DDT and examined or changed in) 1942 SB
225 1706 1948 (preparation for a new generation of the system. DDT is loaded with the memory image by typing: ) 1948 SB
225 1825 1329 (DDT CPMxx.COM         Loads DDT, then reads the CP/M image.) 1329 SB
225 1943 807 (DDT should respond with the following:) 807 SB
225 2061 208 (NEXT PC) 208 SB
225 2120 213 (2300 0100) 213 SB
225 2180 948 (-                                          \(The DDT prompt\)) 948 SB
225 2298 1853 (You can then give the display and disassembly commands to examine portions of the memory) 1853 SB
225 2357 1891 (image between 900H and 227FH.  Note, however, that to find any particular address within the) 1891 SB
225 2416 1910 (memory image, you must apply the negative bias to the CP/M address to find the actual address.) 1910 SB
225 2475 1946 (Track 00, sector 01, is loaded to location 900H \(the user should find the cold start loader at 900H) 1946 SB
225 2535 1788 (to 97FH\); track 00, sector 02, is loaded into 980H \(this is the base of the CCP\); and so on) 1788 SB
225 2594 1941 (through the entire CP/M system load. In a 20K system, for example, the CCP resides at the CP/M) 1941 SB
225 2653 1927 (address 3400H, but is placed into memory at 980H by the SYSGEN program. Thus, the negative) 1927 SB
225 2712 540 (bias, denoted by n, satisfies) 540 SB
