225 227 1841 (This program is assembled and listed in Appendix B for reference purposes, with an assumed) 1841 SB
225 286 1908 (origin of 100H. The hexadecimal operation codes that are listed on the left might be useful if the) 1908 SB
225 345 1076 (program has to be entered through the panel switches.) 1076 SB
225 464 1895 (The PUTSYS program can be constructed from GETSYS by changing only a few operations in) 1895 SB
225 523 1898 (the GETSYS program given above, as shown in Appendix C. The register pair HL becomes the) 1898 SB
225 582 1897 (dump address, next address to write, and operations on these registers do not change within the) 1897 SB
225 641 1947 (program. The READSEC subroutine is replaced by a WRITESEC subroutine, which performs the) 1947 SB
225 700 1851 (opposite function; data from address HL is written to the track given by register B and sector) 1851 SB
225 760 1878 (given by register C. It is often useful to combine GETSYS and PUTSYS into a single program) 1878 SB
225 819 1297 (during the test and development phase, as shown in Appendix C. ) 1297 SB
