225 1351 1929 (The entry points into the BIOS from the cold start loader and BDOS are detailed below. Entry to) 1929 SB
225 1410 1949 (the BIOS is through a jump vector located at 4A00H + b, as shown below. See Appendixes A and) 1949 SB
225 1470 1789 (B. The jump vector is a sequence of 17 jump instructions that send program control to the) 1789 SB
225 1529 1879 (individual BIOS subroutines. The BIOS subroutines might be empty for certain functions \(they) 1879 SB
225 1588 1880 (might contain a single RET operation\) during reconfiguration of CP/M, but the entries must be) 1880 SB
225 1647 544 (present in the jump vector. ) 544 SB
225 1765 1930 (The jump vector at 4A00H + b takes the form shown below, where the individual jump addresses) 1930 SB
225 1825 400 (are given to the left:) 400 SB
225 1943 237 (4A00H+b   ) 237 SB
525 1943 331 (JMP BOOT       ) 331 SB
975 1943 964 (;ARRIVE HERE FROM COLD START LOAD) 964 SB
225 2061 237 (4A03H+b   ) 237 SB
525 2061 364 (JMP WBOOT      ) 364 SB
975 2061 793 (;ARRIVE HERE FOR WARM START) 793 SB
225 2180 237 (4A06H+b   ) 237 SB
525 2180 346 (JMP CONST      ) 346 SB
975 2180 867 (;CHECK FOR CONSOLE CHAR READY) 867 SB
