225 2002 1900 (Each jump address corresponds to a particular subroutine that performs the specific function, as) 1900 SB
225 2061 1822 (outlined below. There are three major divisions in the jump table: the system reinitialization,) 1822 SB
225 2120 1843 (which results from calls on BOOT and WBOOT; simple character I/O, performed by calls on) 1843 SB
225 2180 1912 (CONST, CONIN, CONOUT, LIST, PUNCH, READER, and LISTST; and disk I/O, performed) 1912 SB
225 2239 1933 (by calls on HOME, SELDSK, SETTRK, SETSEC, SETDMA, READ, WRITE, and SECTRAN.) 1933 SB
