225 227 1835 (The definition of the IOBYTE function corresponds to the Intel standard as follows: a single) 1835 SB
225 286 1900 (location in memory, currently location 0003H, is maintained, called IOBYTE, which defines the) 1900 SB
225 345 1929 (logical-to-physical device mapping that is in effect at a particular time. The mapping is performed) 1929 SB
225 405 1752 (by splitting the IOBYTE into four distinct fields of two bits each, called the CONSOLE,) 1752 SB
225 464 1403 (READER, PUNCH, and LIST fields, as shown in the following figure.) 1403 SB
225 582 1232 (               MOST SIGNIFICANT       LEAST SIGNIFICANT) 1232 SB
225 700 1312 (IOBYTE AT 003H LIST       PUNCH     READER    CONSOLE) 1312 SB
225 819 1026 (               BITS  6,7  BITS 4,5  BITS 2,3  BITS 0,1) 1026 SB
225 937 808 (                    Figure 6-1. IOBYTE Fields) 808 SB
225 1055 1938 (The value in each field can be in the range 0-3, defining the assigned source or destination of each) 1938 SB
225 1115 1493 (logical device. Table 6-4 gives the values that can be assigned to each field.) 1493 SB
869 1233 661 (Table 6-4. IOBYTE Field Values) 661 SB
