225 227 1915 (The READ and WRITE routines should perform several retries \(10 is standard\) before reporting) 1915 SB
225 286 1881 (the error condition to the BDOS.  If the error condition is returned to the BDOS, it reports the) 1881 SB
225 345 1897 (error to the user. The HOME subroutine might or might not actually perform the track 00 seek,) 1897 SB
225 405 1891 (depending upon controller characteristics; the important point is that track 00 has been selected) 1891 SB
225 464 1765 (for the next operation and is often treated in exactly the same manner as SETTRK with a) 1765 SB
225 523 329 (parameter of 00.) 329 SB
225 641 1826 (The following table describes the exact responsibilities of each BIOS entry point subroutine.) 1826 SB
898 819 604 (Table 6-5.  BIOS Entry Points) 604 SB
