225 1055 201 (     BOOT) 201 SB
675 1055 1363 (The BOOT entry point gets control from the cold start loader and is ) 1363 SB
675 1115 1387 (responsible for basic system initialization, including sending a sign-on ) 1387 SB
675 1174 1491 (message, which can be omitted in the first version. If the IOBYTE function) 1491 SB
675 1233 1488 (is implemented, it must be set at this point. The various system parameters ) 1488 SB
675 1292 1457 (that are set by the WBOOT entry point must be initialized, and control is ) 1457 SB
675 1351 1361 (transferred to the CCP at 3400 + b for further processing. Note that ) 1361 SB
675 1410 939 (register C must be set to zero to select drive A.) 939 SB
225 1529 247 (     WBOOT) 247 SB
675 1529 1473 (The WBOOT entry point gets control when a warm start occurs. A warm ) 1473 SB
675 1588 1499 (start is performed whenever a user program branches to location 0000H, or) 1499 SB
675 1647 1416 (when the CPU is reset from the front panel. The CP/M system must be ) 1416 SB
675 1706 1422 (loaded from the first two tracks of drive A up to, but not including, the ) 1422 SB
675 1765 1472 (BIOS, or CBIOS, if the user has completed the patch. System parameters ) 1472 SB
675 1825 585 (must be initialized as follows:) 585 SB
225 1943 195 (               ) 195 SB
675 1943 273 (location 0,1,2) 273 SB
