225 464 195 (               ) 195 SB
675 464 273 (location 5,6,7) 273 SB
1125 464 1039 (Set to JMP BDOS, which is the primary entry point ) 1039 SB
1125 523 938 (to CP/M for transient programs. \(0005H: JMP ) 938 SB
1125 582 239 (3C06H + b\)) 239 SB
675 700 1296 (Refer to Section 6.9 for complete details of page zero use. Upon ) 1296 SB
675 760 1464 (completion of the initialization, the WBOOT program must branch to the ) 1464 SB
675 819 1494 (CCP at 3400H + b to restart the system. Upon entry to the CCP, register C) 1494 SB
675 878 1492 (is set to the drive to select after system initialization. The WBOOT routine ) 1492 SB
675 937 1492 (should read location 4 in memory, verify that is a legal drive, and pass it to ) 1492 SB
675 996 438 (the CCP in register C.) 438 SB
225 1115 229 (     CONST) 229 SB
675 1115 1483 (You should sample the status of the currently assigned console device and ) 1483 SB
675 1174 1491 (return 0FFH in register A if a character is ready to read and 00H in register) 1491 SB
675 1233 726 (A if no console characters are ready.) 726 SB
225 1351 223 (     CONIN) 223 SB
675 1351 1479 (The next console character is read into register A, and the parity bit is set, ) 1479 SB
675 1410 1360 (high-order bit, to zero.  If no console character is ready, wait until a ) 1360 SB
675 1470 696 (character is typed before returning.) 696 SB
225 1588 273 (     CONOUT) 273 SB
675 1588 1418 (The character is sent from register C to the console output device. The ) 1418 SB
675 1647 1420 (character is in ASCII, with high-order parity bit set to zero. You might ) 1420 SB
675 1706 1470 (want to include a time-out on a line-feed or carriage return, if the console ) 1470 SB
675 1765 1491 (device requires some time interval at the end of the line \(such as a TI Silent) 1491 SB
675 1825 1478 (700 terminal\). You can filter out control characters that cause the console ) 1478 SB
675 1884 1493 (device to react in a strange way \(CTRL-Z causes the Lear-Siegler terminal ) 1493 SB
675 1943 653 (to clear the screen, for example\).) 653 SB
225 2061 171 (     LIST) 171 SB
675 2061 1370 (The character is sent from register C to the currently assigned listing ) 1370 SB
675 2120 1066 (device. The character is in ASCII with zero parity bit.) 1066 SB
225 2239 234 (     PUNCH) 234 SB
675 2239 1371 (The character is sent from register C to the currently assigned punch ) 1371 SB
675 2298 1002 (device. The character is in ASCII with zero parity.) 1002 SB
225 2416 264 (     READER) 264 SB
675 2416 1448 (The next character is read from the currently assigned reader device into ) 1448 SB
675 2475 1417 (register A with zero parity \(high-order bit must be zero\); an end-of-file ) 1417 SB
675 2535 1198 (condition is reported by returning an ASCII CTRL-Z\(1AH\).) 1198 SB
