225 464 212 (     HOME) 212 SB
675 464 1452 (The disk head of the currently selected disk \(initially disk A\) is moved to ) 1452 SB
675 523 1420 (the track 00 position.  If the controller allows access to the track 0 flag ) 1420 SB
675 582 1469 (from the drive, the head is stepped until the track 0 flag is detected. If the ) 1469 SB
675 641 1491 (controller does not support this feature, the HOME call is translated into a ) 1491 SB
675 700 776 (call to SETTRK with a parameter of 0.) 776 SB
225 819 253 (     SELDSK) 253 SB
675 819 1488 (The disk drive given by register C is selected for further operations, where ) 1488 SB
675 878 1405 (register C contains 0 for drive A, 1 for drive B, and so on up to 15 for ) 1405 SB
675 937 1470 (drive P \(the standard CP/M distribution version supports four drives\). On ) 1470 SB
675 996 1495 (each disk select, SELDSK must return in HL the base address of a 16-byte ) 1495 SB
675 1055 1410 (area, called the Disk Parameter Header, described in Section 6.10. For ) 1410 SB
675 1115 1388 (standard floppy disk drives, the contents of the header and associated ) 1388 SB
675 1174 1429 (tables do not change; thus, the program segment included in the sample ) 1429 SB
675 1233 914 (CBIOS performs this operation automatically.) 914 SB
675 1351 1478 (If there is an attempt to select a nonexistent drive, SELDSK returns HL = ) 1478 SB
675 1410 1436 (0000H as an error indicator. Although SELDSK must return the header ) 1436 SB
675 1470 1415 (address on each call, it is advisable to postpone the physical disk select ) 1415 SB
675 1529 1491 (operation until an I/O function \(seek, read, or write\) is actually performed, ) 1491 SB
675 1588 1430 (because disk selects often occur without ultimately performing any disk ) 1430 SB
675 1647 1390 (I/O, , and many controllers unload the head of the current disk before ) 1390 SB
675 1706 1490 (selecting the new drive. This causes an excessive amount of noise and disk ) 1490 SB
675 1765 1331 (wear. The least significant bit of register E is zero if this is the first ) 1331 SB
675 1825 1245 (occurrence of the drive select since the last cold or warm start.) 1245 SB
225 1943 254 (     SETTRK) 254 SB
675 1943 1499 (Register BC contains the track number for subsequent disk accesses on the ) 1499 SB
675 2002 1361 (currently selected drive. The sector number in BC is the same as the ) 1361 SB
675 2061 1494 (number returned from the SECTRAN entry point. You can choose to seek ) 1494 SB
675 2120 1483 (the selected track at this time or delay the seek until the next read or write ) 1483 SB
675 2180 1322 (actually occurs.  Register BC can take on values in the range 0-76 ) 1322 SB
675 2239 1456 (corresponding to valid track numbers for standard floppy disk drives and ) 1456 SB
675 2298 836 (0-65535 for nonstandard disk subsystems.) 836 SB
225 92 450 (6.6 BIOS Entry Points) 450 SB
1526 92 649 (CP/M Operating System Manual) 649 SB
