225 464 247 (     SETSEC) 247 SB
675 464 1498 (Register BC contains the sector number, 1 through 26, for subsequent disk ) 1498 SB
675 523 1437 (accesses on the currently selected drive. The sector number in BC is the ) 1437 SB
675 582 1428 (same as the number returned from the SECTRAN entry point. You can ) 1428 SB
675 641 1390 (choose to send this information to the controller at this point or delay ) 1390 SB
675 700 1073 (sector selection until a read or write operation occurs.) 1073 SB
225 819 270 (     SETDMA) 270 SB
675 819 1342 (Register BC contains the DMA \(Disk Memory Access\) address for ) 1342 SB
675 878 1493 (subsequent read or write operations. For example, if B = 00H and C = 80H) 1493 SB
675 937 1433 (when SETDMA is called, all subsequent read operations read their data ) 1433 SB
675 996 1473 (into 80H through 0FFH and all subsequent write operations get their data ) 1473 SB
675 1055 1499 (from 80H through 0FFH, until the next call to SETDMA occurs. The initial) 1499 SB
675 1115 1387 (DMA address is assumed to be 80H. The controller need not actually ) 1387 SB
675 1174 1381 (support Direct Memory Access. If, for example, all data transfers are ) 1381 SB
675 1233 1429 (through I/O ports, the CBIOS that is constructed uses the 128byte area ) 1429 SB
675 1292 1414 (starting at the selected DMA address for the memory buffer during the ) 1414 SB
675 1351 737 (subsequent read or write operations. ) 737 SB
225 1470 200 (     READ) 200 SB
675 1470 1301 (Assuming the drive has been selected, the track has been set, and ) 1301 SB
675 1529 1428 (the DMA address has been specified, the READ subroutine attempts to ) 1428 SB
675 1588 1435 (read eone sector based upon these parameters and returns the following ) 1435 SB
675 1647 499 (error codes in register A:) 499 SB
225 1706 13 ( ) 13 SB
225 1765 65 (     ) 65 SB
675 1765 447 (0    no errors occurred) 447 SB
225 1825 39 (   ) 39 SB
225 1884 65 (     ) 65 SB
675 1884 881 (1    nonrecoverable error condition occurred) 881 SB
225 1943 39 (   ) 39 SB
675 2002 1432 (Currently, CP/M responds only to a zero or nonzero value as the return ) 1432 SB
675 2061 1434 (code. That is, if the value in register A is 0, CP/M assumes that the disk ) 1434 SB
675 2120 1454 (operation was completed properly. IF an error occurs the CBIOS should ) 1454 SB
675 2180 1473 (attempt at least 10 retries to see if the error is recoverable. When an error ) 1473 SB
675 2239 1333 (is reported the BDOS prints the message BDOS ERR ON x: BAD ) 1333 SB
675 2298 1493 (SECTOR. The operator then has the option of pressing a carriage return to) 1493 SB
675 2357 755 (ignore the error, or CTRL-C to abort.) 755 SB
