225 464 223 (     WRITE) 223 SB
675 464 1458 (Data is written from the currently selected DMA address to the currently ) 1458 SB
675 523 1378 (selected drive, track, and sector. For floppy disks, the data should be ) 1378 SB
675 582 1396 (marked as nondeleted data to maintain compatibility with other CP/M ) 1396 SB
675 641 1409 (systems. The error codes given in the READ command are returned in ) 1409 SB
675 700 1190 (register A, with error recovery attempts as described above.) 1190 SB
225 819 230 (     LISTST) 230 SB
675 819 1372 (You return the ready status of the list device used by the DESPOOL ) 1372 SB
675 878 1493 (program to improve console response during its operation. The value 00 is ) 1493 SB
675 937 1484 (returned in A if the list device is not ready to accept a character and 0FFH ) 1484 SB
675 996 1455 (if a character can be sent to the printer.  A 00 value should be returned if ) 1455 SB
675 1055 635 (LIST status is not implemented.) 635 SB
225 1174 292 (     SECTRAN) 292 SB
675 1174 1466 (Logical-to-physical sector translation is performed to improve the overall ) 1466 SB
675 1233 1495 (response of CP/M. Standard CP/M systems are shipped with a skew factor ) 1495 SB
675 1292 1396 (of 6, where six physical sectors are skipped between each logical read ) 1396 SB
675 1351 1469 (operation. This skew factor allows enough time between sectors for most ) 1469 SB
675 1410 1495 (programs to load their buffers without missing the next sector. In particular) 1495 SB
675 1470 1473 (computer systems that use fast processors, memory, and disk subsystems, ) 1473 SB
675 1529 1468 (the skew factor might be changed to improve overall response. However, ) 1468 SB
675 1588 1498 (the user should maintain a single-density IBM-compatible version of CP/M ) 1498 SB
675 1647 1490 (for information transfer into and out of the computer system, using a skew ) 1490 SB
675 1706 222 (factor of 6.) 222 SB
675 1825 1474 (In general, SECTRAN receives a logical sector number relative to zero in ) 1474 SB
675 1884 1438 (BC and a translate table address in DE. The sector number is used as an ) 1438 SB
675 1943 1461 (index into the translate table, with the resulting physical sector number in ) 1461 SB
675 2002 1448 (HL. For standard systems, the table and indexing code is provided in the ) 1448 SB
675 2061 664 (CBIOS and need not be changed.) 664 SB
225 92 450 (6.6 BIOS Entry Points) 450 SB
1526 92 649 (CP/M Operating System Manual) 649 SB
