225 227 587 (6.10 Disk Parameter Tables) 587 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
225 345 1908 (Tables are included in the BIOS that describe the particular characteristics of the disk subsystem) 1908 SB
225 405 1795 (used with CP/M. These tables can be either hand-coded, as shown in the sample CBIOS in) 1795 SB
225 464 1947 (Appendix B, or automatically generated using the DISKDEF macro library, as shown in Appendix) 1947 SB
225 523 1243 (F. The purpose here is to describe the elements of these tables.) 1243 SB
225 641 1790 (In general, each disk drive has an associated \(16-byte\) disk parameter header that contains) 1790 SB
225 700 1871 (information about the disk drive and provides a scratch pad area for certain BDOS operations.) 1871 SB
225 760 1794 (The format of the disk parameter header for each drive is shown in Figure 6-2, where each) 1794 SB
225 819 646 (element is a word \(16-bit\) value.) 646 SB
225 937 931 (                      DISK PARAMETER HEADER) 931 SB
225 996 1269 (     +-------+------+------+------+----------+-------+-------+-------+) 1269 SB
225 1055 1263 (     | XLT  | 0000 | 0000 | 0000 |DIRBUF| DPB  | CSV  | ALV  |) 1263 SB
225 1115 1269 (     +------+------+------+-------+----------+-------+-------+-------+) 1269 SB
225 1174 1119 (       16B    16B    16B    16B    16B    16B    16B    16B) 1119 SB
773 1292 855 (Figure 6-2. Disk Parameter Header Format) 855 SB
225 1410 1682 (The meaning of each Disk Parameter Header \(DPH\) element is detailed in Table 6-7.) 1682 SB
844 1529 713 (Table 6-7.  Disk Parameter Headers) 713 SB
225 1647 346 (   Disk Parameter) 346 SB
