225 227 1904 (Position 00 corresponds to the high-order bit of the byte labeled AL0 and 15 corresponds to the) 1904 SB
225 286 1819 (low-order bit of the byte labeled AL1. Each bit position reserves a data block for number of) 1819 SB
225 345 1908 (directory entries, thus allowing a total of 16 data blocks to be assigned for directory entries \(bits) 1908 SB
225 405 1916 (are assigned starting at 00 and filled to the right until position 15\). Each directory entry occupies) 1916 SB
225 464 911 (32 bytes, resulting in the following tabulation:) 911 SB
920 641 559 (Table 6-10. BLS Tabulation) 559 SB
525 760 221 (                 ) 221 SB
32 0 0 50 50 1 0 1 45 /MSTT31c322 font
746 760 512 (BLS      Directory Entries) 512 SB
