225 227 1839 (The size of the area addressed by CSV is CKS bytes, which is sufficient to hold the directory) 1839 SB
225 286 1862 (check information for this particular drive. If CKS = \(DRM + 1\)/4, you must reserve \(DRM +) 1862 SB
225 345 1386 (1\)/4 bytes for directory check use. If CKS = 0, no storage is reserved.) 1386 SB
225 464 1845 (The size of the area addressed by ALV is determined by the maximum number of data blocks) 1845 SB
225 523 1283 (allowed for this particular disk and is computed as \(DSM/8\) + 1.) 1283 SB
