0 0 0 fC
225 227 1920 (The cks parameter determines the number of directory items to check on each directory scan and) 1920 SB
225 286 1894 (is used internally to detect changed disks during system operation, where an intervening cold or) 1894 SB
225 345 1915 (warm start has not occurred. When this situation is detected, CP/M automatically marks the disk) 1915 SB
225 405 1068 (Read-Only so that data is not subsequently destroyed.) 1068 SB
225 523 1909 (As stated in the previous section, the value of cks = dir when the medium is easily changed, as is) 1909 SB
225 582 1838 (the case with a floppy disk subsystem. If the disk is permanently mounted, the value of cks is) 1838 SB
225 641 1528 (typically 0, because the probability of changing disks without a restart is low.) 1528 SB
225 760 1850 (The ofs value determines the number of tracks to skip when this particular drive is addressed,) 1850 SB
225 819 1834 (which can be used to reserve additional operating system space or to simulate several logical) 1834 SB
225 878 1862 (drives on a single large capacity physical drive. Finally, the [0] parameter is included when file) 1862 SB
225 937 1858 (compatibility is required with versions of 1.4 that have been modified for higher density disks.) 1858 SB
225 996 1887 (This parameter ensures that only 16K is allocated for each directory record, as was the case for) 1887 SB
225 1055 1193 (previous versions.  Normally, this parameter is not included.) 1193 SB
225 1174 1245 (For convenience and economy of table space, the special form:) 1245 SB
225 1292 286 (DISKDEF   i,j) 286 SB
225 1410 1758 (gives disk i the same characteristics as a previously defined drive j. A standard fourdrive,) 1758 SB
225 1470 1915 (single-density system, which is compatible with version 1.4, is defined using the following macro) 1915 SB
225 1529 240 (invocations:) 240 SB
225 1647 247 (DISKS      4) 247 SB
225 1706 728 (DISKDEF    0,1,26,6,1024,243,64,2) 728 SB
225 1765 325 (DISKDEF    1,0) 325 SB
225 1825 325 (DISKDEF    2,0) 325 SB
225 1884 325 (DISKDEF    3,0) 325 SB
225 1943 208 (          ......) 208 SB
225 2002 161 (ENDEF) 161 SB
225 2120 1905 (with all disks having the same parameter values of 26 sectors per track, numbered 1 through 26,) 1905 SB
225 2180 1950 (with 6 sectors skipped between each access, 1024 bytes per data block, 243 data blocks for a total) 1950 SB
225 2239 1804 (of 243K-byte disk capacity, 64 checked directory entries, and two operating system tracks.) 1804 SB
