225 227 1903 (The DISKS macro generates n DPHS, starting at the DPH table address DPBASE generated by) 1903 SB
225 286 1860 (the macro. Each disk header block contains sixteen bytes, as described above, and correspond) 1860 SB
225 345 1843 (one-for-one to each of the defined drives. In the four-drive standard system, for example, the) 1843 SB
225 405 875 (DISKS macro generates a table of the form:) 875 SB
225 523 345 (DPBASE EQU $) 345 SB
375 582 1439 (DPEO:  DW XLT0,0000H,0000H,0000H,DIRBUF,DPB0,CSV0,ALV0) 1439 SB
375 641 1428 (DPE1:  DW XLT0,0000H,0000H,0000H,DIRBUF,DPB0,CSV1,ALV1) 1428 SB
375 700 1428 (DPE2:  DW XLT0,0000H,0000H,0000H,DIRBUF,DPB0,CSV2,ALV2) 1428 SB
375 760 1428 (DPE3:  DW XLT0,0000H,0000H,0000H,DIRBUF,DPB0,CSV3,ALV3) 1428 SB
225 878 1906 (where the DPH labels are included for reference purposes to show the beginning table addresses) 1906 SB
225 937 1855 (for each drive 0 through 3. The values contained within the DPH are described in detail in the) 1855 SB
225 996 1912 (previous section. The check and allocation vector addresses are generated by the ENDEF macro) 1912 SB
225 1055 1065 (in the RAM area following the BIOS code and tables.) 1065 SB
225 1174 1814 (Note that if the skf \(skew factor\) parameter is omitted, or equal to 0, the translation table is) 1814 SB
225 1233 1738 (omitted and a 0000H value is inserted in the XLT position of the DPH for the disk. In a) 1738 SB
225 1292 1882 (subsequent call to perform the logical-to-physical translation, SECTRAN receives a translation) 1882 SB
225 1351 1862 (table address of DE = 0000H and simply returns the original logical sector from BC in the HL) 1862 SB
225 1410 251 (register pair.) 251 SB
225 1529 1940 (A translate table is constructed when the skf parameter is present, and the \(nonzero\) table address) 1940 SB
225 1588 1834 (is placed into the corresponding DPHS. The following, for example, is constructed when the) 1834 SB
225 1647 1374 (standard skew factor skf = 6 is specified in the DISKDEF macro call:) 1374 SB
375 1765 149 (XLT0: ) 149 SB
525 1765 776 (DB 1,7,13,19,25,5,11,17,23,3,9,15,21 ) 776 SB
225 1825 78 (      ) 78 SB
525 1825 788 (DB 2,8,14,20,26,6,12,18,24,4,10,16,22) 788 SB
