225 286 465 (                ;MODIFIED) 465 SB
225 345 1725 (                ;RESIDES ON TRACK 00, SECTOR 01 \(THE FIRST SECTOR ON THE ) 1725 SB
225 405 1737 (                ;DISKETTE\), WE ASSUME THAT THE CONTROLLER HAS LOADED ) 1737 SB
225 464 1675 (                ;THIS SECTOR INTO MEMORY UPON SYSTEM START-UP \(THIS ) 1675 SB
225 523 1662 (                ;PROGRAM CAN BE KEYED-IN, OR CAN EXIST IN READ-ONLY ) 1662 SB
225 582 445 (                ;MEMORY) 445 SB
225 641 1743 (                ;BEYOND THE ADDRESS SPACE OF THE CP/M VERSION YOU ARE ) 1743 SB
225 700 1788 (                ;RUNNING\). THE COLD START LOADER BRINGS THE CP/M SYSTEM ) 1788 SB
225 760 1477 (                ;INTO MEMORY AT"LOADP" \(3400H +"BIAS"\). IN A 20K ) 1477 SB
225 819 1541 (                ;MEMORY SYSTEM, THE VALUE OF"BIAS" IS 000H, WITH ) 1541 SB
225 878 386 (                ;LARGE) 386 SB
225 937 1629 (                ;VALUES FOR INCREASED MEMORY SIZES \(SEE SECTION 2\). ) 1629 SB
225 996 378 (                ;AFTER) 378 SB
225 1055 1571 (                ;LOADING THE CP/M SYSTEM, THE COLD START LOADER ) 1571 SB
225 1115 486 (                ;BRANCHES) 486 SB
225 1174 1710 (                ;TO THE "BOOT" ENTRY POINT OF THE BIOS, WHICH BEGINS AT) 1710 SB
225 1233 1659 (                ; "BIOS" +"BIAS". THE COLD START LOADER IS NOT USED UN-) 1659 SB
225 1292 1749 (                ;TIL THE SYSTEM IS POWERED UP AGAIN, AS LONG AS THE BIOS ) 1749 SB
225 1351 1751 (                ;IS NOT OVERWRITTEN. THE ORIGIN IS ASSUMED AT 0000H, AND ) 1751 SB
225 1410 1842 (                ;MUST BE CHANGED IF THE CONTROLLER BRINGS THE COLD START ) 1842 SB
225 1470 1706 (                ;LOADER INTO ANOTHER AREA, OR IF A READ-ONLY MEMORY ) 1706 SB
