225 2128 1809 (CP/M system. It provides the BDOS with a set of primitive I/O operations. The BIOS is an) 1809 SB
225 2187 1872 (assembly language module usually written by the user, hardware manufacturer, or independent) 1872 SB
225 2246 1950 (software vendor, and is the key to CP/M's portability. The BIOS interfaces the CP/M system to its) 1950 SB
225 2305 1859 (hardware environment through a standardized jump table at the front of the BIOS routine and) 1859 SB
225 2364 1778 (through a set of disk parameter tables which define the disk environment. Thus, the BIOS) 1778 SB
225 2424 1156 (provides CP/M with a completely table-driven I/O system.) 1156 SB
