946 1297 1160 ( In some disk subsystems the disk sector size is larger than) 1160 SB
225 1356 1861 (128 bytes, usually 256, 512, 1024, or 2048 bytes. When the host sector size is larger than 128) 1861 SB
225 1416 1905 (bytes, host sectors must be buffered in memory and the 128-byte CP/M sectors must be blocked) 1905 SB
225 1475 1911 (and deblocked by adding an additional module, the blocking and deblocking  algorithm, between) 1911 SB
225 1534 1925 (the BIOS disk I/O routines and the actual disk I/O. The host sector size must be an even multiple) 1925 SB
225 1593 1909 (of 128 bytes for the algorithm to work correctly.  The blocking and deblocking algorithm allows) 1909 SB
225 1652 1946 (the BDOS and BIOS to function exactly as if the entire disk consisted only of 128-byte sectors, as) 1946 SB
225 1711 665 (in the standard CP/M installation.) 665 SB
