337 1950 1763 ( Process of loading an operating system into memory. A boot program is a small piece of) 1763 SB
225 2009 1785 (code that is automatically executed when you power-up or reset your computer. The boot) 1785 SB
225 2069 1810 (program loads the rest of the operating system into memory in a manner similar to a person) 1810 SB
225 2128 1860 (pulling himself up by his own bootstraps. This process is sometimes called a cold boot or cold) 1860 SB
225 2187 1893 (start. Bootstrap pocedures vary from system to system.  The boot program must be customized) 1893 SB
225 2246 1941 (for the memory size and hardware environment that the operating system manages.  Typically, the) 1941 SB
225 2305 1943 (boot resides on the first sector of the system tracks on your system disk. When executed, the boot) 1943 SB
225 2364 1883 (loads the remaining sectors of the system tracks into high memory at the location for which the) 1883 SB
225 2424 1936 (CP/M system has been configured.  Finally, the boot transfers execution to the boot entry point in) 1936 SB
225 2483 1922 (the BIOS jump table so that the system can initialize itself.  In this case, the boot program should) 1922 SB
225 2542 1837 (be placed at 900H in the SYSGEN image. Alternatively, the boot program may be located in) 1837 SB
225 2601 126 (ROM.) 126 SB
