344 1061 1761 ( Console Command Processor. The CCP is a module of the CP/M operating system. It is) 1761 SB
225 1120 1841 (loaded directly below the BDOS module and interprets and executes commands typed by the) 1841 SB
225 1179 1758 (console user.  Usually these commands are programs that the CCP loads and calls. Upon) 1758 SB
225 1238 1892 (completion, a command program may return control to the CCP if it has not overwritten it. If it) 1892 SB
225 1297 1916 (has, the program can reload the CCP into memory by a warm boot operation initiated by either a) 1916 SB
225 1356 1848 (jump to zero, BDOS system reset \(Function 0\), or a cold boot. Except for its location in high) 1848 SB
225 1416 1852 (memory, the CCP works like any other standard CP/M program; that is, it makes only BDOS) 1852 SB
225 1475 707 (function calls for its I/O operations.) 707 SB
