743 1832 1347 ( Contiguous data area in the BIOS, with one byte for each directory) 1347 SB
225 1891 1740 (sector to be checked, that is, CKS bytes. See CKS. A checksum vector is initialized and) 1740 SB
225 1950 1876 (maintained for each logged-in drive. Each directory access by the system results in a checksum) 1876 SB
225 2009 1869 (calculation that is compared with the one in the checksum vector. If there is a discrepancy, the) 1869 SB
225 2069 1929 (drive is set to Read-Only status. This feature prevents the user from inadvertently switching disks) 1929 SB
225 2128 1910 (without logging in the new disk. If the new disk is not logged-in, it is treated the same as the old) 1910 SB
225 2187 1122 (one, and data on it might be destroyed if writing is done.) 1122 SB
