341 1594 1754 ( Transient Program Area. Area in memory where user programs run and store data. This) 1754 SB
225 1653 1909 (area is a region of memory beginning at 0100H and extending to the base of the CP/M system in) 1909 SB
225 1713 1869 (high memory. The first module of the CP/M system is the CCP, which can be overwritten by a) 1869 SB
225 1772 1888 (user program. If so, the TPA is extended to the base of the CP/M BDOS module. If the CCP is) 1888 SB
225 1831 1851 (overwritten, the user program must terminate with either a system reset \(Function 0\) call or a) 1851 SB
225 1890 1810 (jump to location zero in page zero. The address of the base of the CP/M BDOS is stored in) 1810 SB
